d recent tournament results for Ilbirs suggest potential organizational or roster instability"], "key_context": ["Match is part of EPL Group A, a Tier 3 European competitive circuit", "Data from February-March 2026 shows Ilbirs competing in EPL Championship Season 2", "Search results contain limited information about BALU's roster, recent form, or head-to-head record with Ilbirs", "No explicit head-to-head match history between Ilbirs eSports and BALU found in provided results", "BO3 format requires winning 2 maps, making individual map performance critical"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:43:59.400775Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T13:40:41.383155+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "correct_pass", "summary": "Correct PASS \u2014 council was unsure, median prob 62%; winner was YES", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.68, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports' demonstrated map-winning capability and EPL experience against an opponent with minimal competitive visibility in recent tournament records."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.62, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.62, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "Ilbirs eSports shows volatile form (2:0 wins, 0:2 losses, 1:2 close defeats within 4 days in late February) typical of mid-tier Tier 3 rosters with inconsistent meta adaptation; BALU's near-complete absence from the provided competitive record creates asymmetric information favoring market-implied underdog status."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.62, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "In BO3 Dota 2 matches between teams of disparate competitive tier and visibility, the team with more recent tournament experience and documented wins typically wins 60-70% of the time; however, asymmetric information on opponent strength introduces significant uncertainty."}, {"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.58, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.42, "key_factor": "Critically insufficient data on BALU's roster, recent performance, and competitive level makes reliable probability assessment impossible; market prices suggest confidence in Ilbirs that cannot be justified from briefing data."}], "agents_against_winner": [{"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.42, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.28, "key_factor": "BALU executes a pre-planned meta counter-strategy or brings in a stand-in player who exploits Ilbirs' recent map pool vulnerabilities that the briefing entirely omits."}], "median_prob": 0.62, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "8adde437-5907-4739-95ff-e0b042e24c7a", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:45:11.512706+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1883072", "question": "Counter-Strike: Abyssal vs Ground Zero (BO3) - ESL Challenger League Oceania Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between Abyssal and Ground Zero in the ESL Challenger League Oceania Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Abyssal\" if Abyssal win the match against Ground Zero.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ground Zero\" if Ground Zero win the match against Abyssal.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 8500.92114, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Event timing is TODAY with ~5 hours to resolution; match is imminent and outcome will be determined by actual play. Market currently prices YES (Abyssal) at 55% and NO (Ground Zero) at 45%, indicating slight market lean toward Abyssal. Resolution criteria are clear: match resolves to winning team if completed normally; 50-50 only if canceled, forfeited pre-start, or delayed >7 days. Abyssal stat advantage: 1.12 rating vs Ground Zero's 1.08 rating (3-month period); 71.3% KAST vs 74.5% KAST suggests Abyssal slightly more effective in fragging despite Ground Zero's marginally better map control efficiency. Abyssal weaknesses: 0.73 KPR and 0.68 DPR indicate below-average kill and death rates, potential vulnerability in sustained duels. Ground Zero recent playoff exposure: competed in Cup #2 against Rooster (lost 1-2), providing recent tournament pressure experience. Both teams are regional Oceania-level competitors; neither has documented dominant regional standing or recent dominant win streaks in briefing. Head-to-head history unavailable in briefing; no direct precedent to inform probability beyond individual stat comparisons. Briefing notes both teams 'struggling against' Rooster, suggesting relatively balanced regional tier without clear hierarchy. LAN format (high-stakes, no latency issues) favors teams with superior raw mechanics; Abyssal's marginal rating advantage may hold in direct competition. Confidence limited by: (1) sparse competitive data for both teams, (2) no recent BO3 results for either, (3) roster roster stability unknown, (4) regional tournament data not comprehensive. Market price of 55-45 appears reasonable given stat parity; slight Abyssal lean supported by marginal rating edge but not overwhelming. Probability set to 55 to reflect mild statistical edge for Abyssal while acknowledging high uncertainty; confidence scores low (42/38) due to data scarcity on both sides.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive history and team roster stability data between Abyssal and Ground Zero prevents high-confidence assessment; both teams are regional-level competitors with limited public performance documentation."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "ABYSSAL'S STATISTICAL EDGE: Abyssal holds a 1.12 rating over 3 months vs Ground Zero's 1.08\u2014a small but measurable individual performance advantage in a LAN environment where consistency matters. GROUND ZERO'S RECENT LOSS: Ground Zero lost 1-2 to Rooster in Cup #2, indicating vulnerability under playoff pressure and potentially shaken confidence entering this Upper Bracket Final. KAST EFFICIENCY PARADOX: While Ground Zero shows 74.5% KAST vs Abyssal's 71.3%, Abyssal compensates with higher raw rating, suggesting better impact kills and round-closing ability despite slightly lower participation. ABYSSAL'S FRAGGING CONCERN: Abyssal's 0.73 KPR and 0.68 DPR are notably lower than Ground Zero's implied stats, creating real vulnerability in individual duels\u2014this is Ground Zero's strongest counter-argument. LAN FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best of 3 on LAN reduces variance; Abyssal's marginally superior rating (1.12) becomes more predictive in a high-fidelity competitive setting vs online play. PLAYOFF INEXPERIENCE UNKNOWN: Briefing provides no head-to-head history or Abyssal's recent playoff trajectory, creating symmetric information gaps\u2014both teams are regional-level competitors with incomplete public data. MARKET PRICING RATIONAL: YES at 55% reflects modest Abyssal favoritism, consistent with their slight statistical edge; this is not an overpriced consensus but rather balanced pricing. GROUND ZERO'S COUNTERPLAY: Recent Rooster exposure and their superior KAST (74.5%) suggest Ground Zero understands playoff meta and may exploit Abyssal's lower KPR through disciplined team play. TIME-SENSITIVE CONSTRAINT: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours\u2014no meaningful new information or roster changes will emerge; market pricing should reflect current data only. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Higher confidence in YES assessment (58) due to direct statistical data; lower confidence in NO (52) because Ground Zero's counter-narrative (momentum, experience) relies on inference from single recent loss rather than quantified advantages.", "key_factor": "Abyssal's superior individual rating (1.12 vs 1.08) and demonstrated KAST efficiency (71.3%) combined with Ground Zero's recent playoff loss to Rooster, suggesting momentum disadvantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Ground Zero's efficiency advantage is material: 74.5% KAST (round participation) vs Abyssal's 71.3% is a 3.2pp edge. In BO3 LAN play, teams that stay alive and win rounds consistently beat teams with flashy stats but lower round participation. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Ground Zero's 1.08 rating is only 0.04 behind Abyssal's 1.12, making the 'rating gap' negligible. The market may be overweighting Abyssal's marginal advantage when efficiency metrics favor Ground Zero. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Recent playoff experience matters in BO3 formats. Ground Zero competed in Cup #2 playoffs just days ago (April 1), while Abyssal's recent playoff trajectory is opaque. Ground Zero has fresh familiarity with pressure and map-veto strategy. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Abyssal's 0.73 KPR and 0.68 DPR are weak points the briefing explicitly highlights. These low fragging metrics suggest individual duels could favor Ground Zero, especially in high-pressure playoff moments. FAVORITE FRAGILITY \u2014 The market's 55% YES price assumes Abyssal's 1.12 rating translates to playoff dominance, but the briefing shows 'mixed individual statistics' and doesn't report recent wins. A 1.12 rating is solid but not exceptional for a regional favorite. FAVORITE FRAGILITY \u2014 Abyssal lacks documented recent playoff success; the briefing provides no evidence of Cup #2 performance or head-to-head history. The 55% price may reflect narrative confidence rather than data. FAVORITE FRAGILITY \u2014 Both teams recently lost to Rooster (implicitly or directly), suggesting neither is dominant. If Rooster is the clear regional power, Abyssal and Ground Zero are likely closer in skill than 55/45 reflects. MARKET BIAS \u2014 YES is priced at 55% with only $8,501 volume, suggesting shallow liquidity and potential narrative-driven mispricing. Underdog NO value often peaks in thin regional esports markets. EVENT TIMING CAUTION \u2014 Match resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). No pre-match adjustments or late roster changes are observable in the briefing. This is a pure statistical matchup with minimal time for new information. DUAL EVALUATION \u2014 YES strengths (Texta/Crunchy/zune experience, 1.12 rating, 71.3% KAST) are real but not overwhelming. NO strengths (74.5% KAST efficiency, 1.08 rating, recent playoff seasoning) are underpriced relative to the gap. CONCLUSION \u2014 Ground Zero is the true underdog at 45%, but efficiency-first teams in BO3 LAN formats win at higher rates than flashy teams. The 55/45 split misvalues the NO side's structural advantages in a best-of series where consistency and round control dominate.", "key_factor": "Ground Zero's superior efficiency metrics (74.5% KAST vs 71.3%, 1.08 vs 1.12 rating) and recent playoff exposure provide a hidden edge that the market undervalues in a BO3 format where consistency wins."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.37, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. Insufficient time for reversals. Market price of 55% YES / 45% NO suggests modest confidence in Abyssal, consistent with statistical noise in regional play. BASE-RATE ANALYSIS: This is an Oceania regional qualifier match (ESL Challenger League Season 51). No reliable historical baseline exists for Abyssal vs Ground Zero head-to-head performance. Regional BO3 playoff matches typically exhibit high variance due to small sample sizes and roster volatility. ABYSSAL CASE: Slightly higher rating (1.12 vs 1.08), lower KAST (71.3% vs 74.5% suggests less efficiency despite higher kills/deaths ratio). Individual stats marginally favor Abyssal but margin is negligible. Roster includes Texta, Crunchy, zune with regional experience. GROUND ZERO CASE: Superior KAST (74.5%) indicates better map control and round efficiency. Recent playoff exposure vs Rooster (lost 1-2) demonstrates competitive readiness. However, recent loss suggests vulnerability against stronger opponents. DATA GAPS: No direct head-to-head history provided. No recent Abyssal playoff results shown. Team consistency, coach impact, and map preparation unknown. Briefing contains substantial noise (unrelated player transfers, incomplete player rosters, fragmented tournament data). STATISTICAL PARITY: Both teams exhibit near-identical rating gaps (0.04 difference is within noise margins). KAST differential (3.2 percentage points) is modest. Neither team demonstrates clear dominance. Market price of 55/45 reasonably reflects uncertainty. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: Confidence on both sides is LOW because substantive competitive data is missing. The briefing lacks: recent form trends, head-to-head records, map win rates, or tactical strengths. LAN format reduces online bias but does not substitute for actual performance data. PROBABILITY ANCHOR: Market price (55% YES) aligns with marginal data favor toward Abyssal. Setting probability slightly above market accounts for Abyssal's fractionally higher rating, but LOW confidence reflects data insufficiency on BOTH sides.", "key_factor": "In regional Counter-Strike BO3 playoffs between evenly-matched Oceania teams, favorites win ~55-60% of the time; however, data on these specific rosters is sparse."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price of 55% YES reflects genuine competitive parity between two regional Oceania teams. Abyssal shows marginal statistical edge: 1.12 rating vs Ground Zero's 1.08, but difference is negligible and within noise margin for regional play. Ground Zero's 74.5% KAST outperforms Abyssal's 71.3%, suggesting slightly better round efficiency and decision-making. Abyssal's fragging metrics (0.73 KPR, 0.68 DPR) are notably weaker than typical playoff competitors, potential vulnerability in LAN gunplay. Ground Zero's recent playoff exposure (Cup #2 loss to Rooster) provides competitive conditioning; Abyssal's recent playoff history unclear. Both teams lost/struggled against Rooster, indicating neither has dominant regional standing. BO3 LAN format on short notice (event TODAY in ~5 hours) reduces preparation advantage; both teams equally rushed. No meaningful head-to-head data between current rosters eliminates predictive leverage either direction. Market is NOT overreacting to any signal; 55-45 split accurately reflects statistical marginal edge for Abyssal offset by Ground Zero's playoff experience. LOW confidence on both sides justified: insufficient roster form data, no recent H2H, regional meta unknown, LAN conditions unpredictable. Crowd appears apathetic rather than emotional \u2014 market price is rational consensus rather than panic or irrational exuberance.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.46, "rationale": "Statistical parity: Abyssal's 1.12 rating vs Ground Zero's 1.08 rating represents a negligible 0.04-point difference (3.7% variance)\u2014within noise margin for regional-level teams. KAST efficiency diverges slightly (Abyssal 71.3% vs Ground Zero 74.5%), suggesting Ground Zero converts utility more effectively, but this 3.2-point gap is marginal in BO3 context. Abyssal's fragging power metrics (0.73 KPR, 0.68 DPR) appear lower than Ground Zero's profile, but briefing lacks Ground Zero's explicit KPR/DPR for direct comparison\u2014data asymmetry limits confidence. Ground Zero's recent Cup #2 loss to Rooster (1-2) suggests playoff experience and exposure to high-level pressure, but loss itself indicates vulnerability at that tier. BO3 LAN format amplifies team cohesion, map pool depth, and anti-stratting over individual fragging\u2014neither team's statistical advantage translates reliably to series outcome. Market pricing (YES 55% / NO 45%) reflects 10-point YES favoritism; this aligns with Abyssal's marginal rating advantage but lacks sufficient statistical edge to justify >55% confidence. No head-to-head historical matchup data provided; recent tournament data (Cup #2) is only proxy for current form. Missing critical data: Abyssal's recent playoff trajectory, map veto tendencies, and explicit Ground Zero KPR/DPR metrics prevent high-confidence directional assessment. LAN environment reduces online variance\u2014expect tighter, more tactical play; both rosters' regional status and comparable skill suggest coin-flip territory.", "key_factor": "Both teams exhibit nearly identical statistical profiles (Abyssal 1.12 rating vs Ground Zero 1.08 rating; KAST differential of 3.2 percentage points) in a BO3 LAN format, indicating this is a genuine statistical coin flip with minimal predictive edge from individual metrics alone\u2014map selection and in-game economy management will likely determine outcome."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~5 hours with LAN play imminent; roster/health disruptions are now impossible to predict or publicly verify before match start. BRIEFING SILENCE ON FORM TRAJECTORY: No recent head-to-head history, no playoff pressure data, no mention of Abyssal's actual performance arc in Cup #3 to date \u2014 only aggregate 3-month stats that mask hot/cold streaks. ROSTER FRAGILITY: Abyssal listed as 3-player core (Texta, Crunchy, zune) with minimal depth info; Ground Zero's 5-player roster appears more stable. A single Abyssal player underperforming on LAN could cascade in BO3. KAST VS FRAGGING MISMATCH: Abyssal's 71.3% KAST is strong but 0.73 KPR and 0.68 DPR are notably weak \u2014 suggests dependency on utility/positioning rather than raw firepower. BO3 punishes teams that cannot secure kills when pivots are needed. RECENT CUP #2 EXPOSURE: Ground Zero lost 1-2 to Rooster but *played* in playoffs; Abyssal's Cup #3 run is opaque \u2014 we don't know if they faced Rooster yet, what maps they've won/lost, or which players are performing under actual bracket pressure. LAN PENALTY UNKNOWN: Regional Oceania CS is less professionalized than tier-1; LAN transitions can expose online-heavy teams. Abyssal's recent stats may be inflated by online play. MARKET PRICING MIRRORS UNCERTAINTY: 55\u201345 split suggests analysts are genuinely unsure; this is not a consensus blowout \u2014 any single player performance variance or tactical surprise flips the BO3. ABSENCE OF RECENT VODS: No mention of Cup #3 match footage, recent demos, or team form updates in last 48 hours \u2014 contrasts with major events where recent performances drive confidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY REASONING: High confidence in YES requires Abyssal's stated stats to translate cleanly to BO3 LAN; high confidence in NO requires Ground Zero's Rooster loss to not reflect broader form issues. Neither condition is well-documented.", "key_factor": "A key Abyssal player (Texta or Crunchy) suffers a last-minute illness, connectivity issue, or LAN-day performance collapse, forcing a tactical reshuffle that Ground Zero exploits in the BO3 format."}], "final_score": 0.5156756756756757, "no_score": 0.4896438356164383, "edge": -0.03432432432432431, "no_edge": 0.03964383561643836, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 52% for YES (need \u226560%); YES-side confidence too low: 47% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1883072", "question": "Counter-Strike: Abyssal vs Ground Zero (BO3) - ESL Challenger League Oceania Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket final match between Abyssal and Ground Zero in the ESL Challenger League Oceania Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Abyssal\" if Abyssal win the match against Ground Zero.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ground Zero\" if Ground Zero win the match against Abyssal.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 8500.92114, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Mindfreak matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup 3!", "Rooster matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup 3!", "Best of 3 (LAN) * Swiss round 5 (teams with a 2-2 record).", "Winner advances to playoffs, losing team is eliminated.", "Yes ofcourse the finns know him, I've been watching him since his early fnatic rising days just hoping to see him get to play in higher tiers,", "PGL Astana 2026 Oceania Closed Qualifier \u00b7 Ground Zero vs Abyssal \u00b7 3 maps \u00b7 Anubis, Mirage, Nuke \u00b7 1st of April 2026.", "Complete overview of the Ground Zero vs.", "Abyssal matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup 3!", "The world ranking is based on teams' achievements over the past year (with severe decay in points throughout each month), recent form over the last 2 months and", "Michael 'chelleos' Hawkins\nNew Zealand\nJordan 'SkulL' Newland\nAustralia\nJake 'ju1ces' Hennessy\nAustralia\nAkram 'ADK' Smida\nAustralia\nDaniel 'rekonz' Mort\nAustralia\nMindfreak\n\n|  |  |  |\n --- \n| Matthew 'Texta' O'Rourke AustraliaTexta | Ethan 'Crunchy' Laker AustraliaCrunchy | Jye 'zune' Pollock Australiazune |\n\nMatthew 'Texta' O'Rourke\nAustralia\nEthan 'Crunchy' Laker\nAustralia\nJye 'zune' Pollock\nAustralia\nAbyssal\nAbyssal\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  --- \n| Sharvesh 'dangeR' Saravanan AustraliadangeR | Maclane 'gump' Cross Australiagump | Jayden 'foggers' Graham Australiafoggers | Antony 'Kiyo' Frilingos AustraliaKiyo | Julian 'vinhy' Dinh-Vu Australiavinhy | [...] # RECENT ACTIVITY\n\n# MINIGAME\n\n# TOP 30 TRANSFERS\n\nLucas 'nqz' Soares\npaiN\npaiN\npaiN\npaiN\nKacper 'xKacpersky' Gabara\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nJeorge 'Jeorge'  Endicott\nNRG\nVoca\nVoca\nDominik 'GruBy' Swiderski\nNo team\nFaZe\nFaZe\nFilip 'NEO' Kubski\nFaZe\nFaZe\nNo team\nThumbnail for stream\nMongolia\n\nMongolia\n\nMongolia\n\nOther\n\nOther\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nOther\n\nRussia\n\nOther\n\nUkraine\n\nSweden\n\nUkraine\n\nMongolia\n\nUnited States\n\nFinland\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nPoland\n\nPoland\n\nArgentina\n\nFrance\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nRussia\n\nPortugal\n\nBrazil\n\nBrazil\n\nMongolia\n\nFrance\n\nMongolia\n\nBrazil\n\nRussia\n\nUkraine\n\nRussia\n\nMongolia\n\nOther\n\nOther\n\nGermany\n\nUkraine\n\nRomania\n\nArgentina\n\nUkraine\n\nVietnam\n\nVietnam\n\nSerbia\n\nPoland\n\nFrance\n\nSpain\n\nRussia\n\nPoland [...] Alexander 'Harbor' Debney\nAustralia\nMitchell 'ElephanT' Rahn\nAustralia\nKenan 'Kezza' Alhadweh\nAustralia\nCamille 'camille' Lando\nAustralia\nEthan 'lawlkay' Mistica\nAustralia\nLE-LUX\nLE-LUX\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  --- \n| Seph 'luffy' Iasakul Australialuffy | Tre 'Snaaz' Johnson AustraliaSnaaz | Val 'Val' Fernanda AustraliaVal | Keli 'delkud' O'Halloran Australiadelkud | Jayden 'R3XY' Playle AustraliaR3XY |\n\nSeph 'luffy' Iasakul\nAustralia\nTre 'Snaaz' Johnson\nAustralia\nVal 'Val' Fernanda\nAustralia\nKeli 'delkud' O'Halloran\nAustralia\nJayden 'R3XY' Playle\nAustralia\n\n# HLTV's world ranking of Counter-Strike Teams\n\n## How is the ranking calculated?"], "news_summary": "Abyssal and Ground Zero are set to compete in a Best of 3 match at the ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup #3 Playoffs. Both teams are from the Australian/Oceania region competing in regional-level Counter-Strike competition. Ground Zero recently played Rooster in Cup #2, losing 1-2, while Abyssal's recent performance data shows mixed individual statistics. The match appears to be part of the playoff bracket for the regional qualifier.", "side_yes_case": ["Abyssal roster includes established players like Texta, Crunchy, and zune with regional experience", "Recent HLTV stats show Abyssal with 1.12 rating over past 3 months, indicating solid individual performance", "Ground Zero lost to Rooster 1-2 in recent Cup #2 match, showing vulnerability", "Abyssal's KAST percentage of 71.3% demonstrates consistent round participation and map control"], "side_no_case": ["Ground Zero has proven playoff experience from recent Cup #2 competition", "Ground Zero's individual stats show 1.08 rating with strong KAST at 74.5%, marginally better efficiency", "Abyssal's 0.73 KPR and 0.68 DPR suggest potential vulnerability in fragging power", "Ground Zero's recent competitive exposure provides familiarity with playoff-level pressure", "Limited public information on Abyssal's recent playoff performance trajectory"], "key_context": ["ESL Challenger League Season 51 Oceania Cup #3 is a regional Australian/Oceania qualifier tournament", "Match format is Best of 3 (BO3) played on LAN, indicating high competitive standard", "Both teams are relatively evenly-matched in regional rankings based on available player rosters", "Recent Cup #2 results show Rooster as regional tournament favorite, with both teams struggling against them", "Limited head-to-head historical data available between these specific rosters"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:45:00.380196Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T15:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T17:02:44.346513+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "e10a6802-76f6-4263-a192-7a20b7325ad5", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:46:01.466916+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1896662", "question": "Counter-Strike: B8 vs Inner Circle Esports (BO3) - PGL Bucharest Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 4 match between B8 and Inner Circle Esports in the PGL Bucharest Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"B8\" if B8 win the match against Inner Circle Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle Esports\" if Inner Circle Esports win the match against B8.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:05:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:05:00Z", "yes_price": 0.45, "volume_usd": 583932.716461, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: B8 wins the BO3 match against Inner Circle Esports in Round 4 of PGL Bucharest Group Stage. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides zero information on B8's record, form, or performance at this tournament. This is a severe asymmetry. INNER CIRCLE STRENGTH SIGNAL: Inner Circle defeated FaZe 2-0, demonstrating they can execute at tournament level. However, FaZe's 0-3 record indicates FaZe is performing poorly\u2014a win over a struggling team is weaker evidence than a win over a strong team. INNER CIRCLE CONTEXT: Inner Circle is in the '0-2 pool' after day two, meaning they have 0-2 record themselves before this match. A 2-0 win over FaZe occurred while Inner Circle was 0-2, suggesting they are not consistently strong. B8 UNKNOWN: No data on B8's record, wins, losses, map record, recent form, or head-to-head history. This prevents meaningful probability estimation for the B8 side. BO3 FORMAT IMPLICATIONS: Best-of-3 requires 2 map wins; variance is higher than single-map play. Consistency across multiple maps is required; limited information on either team's map pool or comfort. MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: Market shows 45% YES (B8) vs 55% NO (Inner Circle), suggesting market belief that Inner Circle is favored ~55-45. This is slight favoring of Inner Circle, consistent with their 2-0 win over FaZe. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Without B8 performance data, I cannot justify high confidence in either direction. The 45-55 market split is defensible but lightly evidenced. B8's true strength is opaque; Inner Circle's 2-0 over FaZe is the only concrete signal, but FaZe's weakness limits its predictive power. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are intentionally low (~35-38) because the briefing lacks sufficient information on B8 to make a robust estimate. Inner Circle's 2-0 over FaZe provides some signal, but it is weak (FaZe is 0-3). Probability_score of 42 reflects slight underdog positioning for B8 (market is 45, I am 42), but with very low conviction due to missing B8 data. RESOLUTION MECHANICS: Criteria are clear and unambiguous; teams are reasonably identifiable. No mechanism risk is apparent. The risk is purely predictive uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on B8's actual performance at PGL Bucharest; Inner Circle's strength is inferred only from a FaZe win, which may not be predictive in a BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NO (Inner Circle) is the favored side at 55% market price; advocating for this outcome means B8 is unlikely to win. Inner Circle has CONCRETE evidence of tournament-level performance: they defeated FaZe 2-0 in the SAME tournament, demonstrating execution capability in PGL Bucharest conditions. FaZe's 0-3 elimination record establishes the tournament features significant competitive variance, but critically, Inner Circle beat FaZe decisively\u2014this is not a weak scalp. B8's performance at PGL Bucharest is entirely absent from the briefing: no wins, losses, maps played, or form indicators are documented. This is the underdog's fatal weakness. The briefing explicitly states 'Limited specific information is available about B8's current form or performance at PGL Bucharest'\u2014this data gap heavily favors Inner Circle, whose recent form IS documented. Inner Circle appears to have momentum within the tournament structure; they are not in the 0-2 pool mentioned (which includes FaZe, s1mple, Voca, and BC.Game), suggesting better record advancement. BO3 format requires consistent execution across 2+ maps; Inner Circle has shown they can execute against tournament opposition (FaZe), while B8's map pool, anti-strats, and consistency remain unproven in briefing data. The market prices YES at 45% (B8 underdog) and NO at 55% (Inner Circle favorite)\u2014this aligns with the asymmetric information: Inner Circle has documented tournament success; B8 does not. Contrarians might argue FaZe's weakness inflates Inner Circle's victory, but a 2-0 sweep in a BO3 format is a clean, decisive win regardless of opponent strength\u2014it proves execution. B8's total absence from tournament reporting (no mention in results, pool placement, or form commentary) suggests either early elimination, lower seeding, or unknown competitive standing\u2014all disadvantageous positions entering a BO3 vs. a team with proven wins. Confidence in NO is elevated (72%) due to inner Circle's documented recent form; confidence in YES is suppressed (35%) due to complete absence of B8 performance data, making it impossible to build a credible case for B8 without fabricating evidence. The 55% NO price appears fairly calibrated, possibly even slightly conservative given the data asymmetry favoring Inner Circle.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle's demonstrated 2-0 victory over FaZe in the same tournament establishes concrete current form, while B8's performance remains entirely undocumented in available briefing data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR B8 (YES): The briefing contains ZERO performance data for B8 at PGL Bucharest \u2014 no wins, losses, maps played, or form indicators. This asymmetric information gap is critical: Inner Circle's 2-0 over FaZe looks impressive on paper, but FaZe's 0-3 tournament collapse suggests the tournament has extreme competitive variance, not that Inner Circle is dominant. FAVORITE'S FRAGILITY: Inner Circle's 2-0 win over FaZe is being heavily weighted by the market, but FaZe's season-long misery (noted by karrigan) means beating a broken team in one match is not a reliable predictor of BO3 consistency. The briefing itself notes FaZe was in the '0-2 pool' alongside multiple other teams \u2014 Inner Circle faced an already-defeated opponent, not a top-tier threat. MISSING B8 INTELLIGENCE: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited specific information is available about B8's current form or performance at PGL Bucharest.' This is a RED FLAG for market efficiency. If B8 had strong wins or form data, it would likely appear in tournament coverage. Silence could mean: (a) B8 underperformed and is correctly priced down, OR (b) B8 is a dark horse with limited media coverage but solid preparation for this specific opponent. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: BO3s reward adaptability and consistency across map vetoes/bans. A single 2-0 result (Inner Circle vs. FaZe) does NOT guarantee BO3 mastery. B8 could have favorable map matchups, superior veto strategy, or players with specific anti-Inner-Circle playstyles that aren't visible in the briefing's limited data. TOURNAMENT CHAOS INDICATOR: Multiple teams in the 0-2 pool (s1mple, FaZe, Inner Circle, Voca) suggests unpredictability and volatility. Inner Circle's 2-0 win doesn't separate them from the chaos \u2014 they're still in the competitive mix, not a proven contender. B8's absence from explicitly named struggling teams could indicate they're performing better than the narrative suggests. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes (35) is low because B8 data is truly missing \u2014 we cannot build a strong affirmative case without their actual performance or roster context. confidence_no (38) is also low because Inner Circle's 2-0 is derived from beating FaZe (a known weak link in this tournament), not from dominant form data. Neither side can be evaluated with high confidence. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 48% reflects genuine uncertainty. The market's 55% NO tilt is modest and likely driven by Inner Circle's single 2-0 result. A BO3 between two poorly-reported teams with one known recent win is nearly a coin flip. B8's complete information void makes them slightly undervalued \u2014 they could easily exploit map-pool or preparation advantages. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: B8 prepared a specialized anti-Inner-Circle draft or map strategy (common in BO3 playoff prep). Inner Circle, riding the FaZe win but lacking deep tournament experience in this format, falls apart across maps 2-3. This requires no additional facts beyond the briefing \u2014 just realistic tournament dynamics. MARKET INEFFICIENCY SIGNAL: If B8 is a known CIS team or strong regional competitor with unreported tournament performance, they could be underpriced. The 45% YES price is justified by silence, but silence \u2260 weakness. In a BO3 today, preparation and matchup design matter as much as narrative.", "key_factor": "B8's actual performance and map pool strength at PGL Bucharest remain completely unreported, making the 55% NO favorite vulnerable to an underdog surge if B8 has prepared strong strategies or map selections for this specific BO3 matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Match resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). No reliable pre-match data on B8's current form, map pool, or player performance at PGL Bucharest has been provided. At this proximity to resolution, prediction confidence must be severely constrained by data gaps. INNER CIRCLE POSITIVE SIGNAL: Defeated FaZe 2-0, a ranked team, within the same tournament. This is a concrete recent result indicating competitive readiness and map execution capability. FaZe's 0-3 elimination suggests tournament-wide variation in team quality. B8 DATA GAP \u2014 CRITICAL: Zero specific information provided about B8's PGL Bucharest performance, current roster form, map preparation, or recent results. The briefing explicitly notes 'Limited specific information is available about B8's current form or performance at PGL Bucharest.' This is a major confidence killer for probability estimation. HISTORICAL BASE RATE APPLIED: In Counter-Strike BO3 group stage matches, when one team has demonstrated a strong recent win (2-0 vs. ranked opponent) and the opponent's form is unknown, the demonstrated team wins ~55-60% of the time. However, this baseline applies only with moderate confidence when the opponent is completely uncharacterized. BO3 FORMAT STABILITY: BO3 format (best-of-3 maps) favors consistency and preparation. This reduces variance compared to single-map elimination and makes recent form more predictive. Inner Circle's 2-0 result carries moderate weight. MARKET PRICING NEUTRAL: YES at 45% and NO at 55% reflects near coin-flip expectations with slight lean to Inner Circle. This aligns with the data asymmetry: Inner Circle has a positive signal (2-0 win); B8 has no signal. CONFIDENCE BOTH SIDES LOW: confidence_yes = 28 and confidence_no = 26 reflect the fundamental data gap. We have one team with a recent tournament win but do not know B8's strengths, weaknesses, current roster form, or map pool. Without B8 characterization, neither probability direction can be held with confidence. The market price of 45/55 appears reasonable given available information, but it is not grounded in sufficient comparative data. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT LOGIC: Set probability_score to 48 (slightly favoring NO/Inner Circle) to reflect the one concrete positive signal (Inner Circle's 2-0 win) while acknowledging severe uncertainty. This is marginally lower than the 50-coin-flip baseline because Inner Circle demonstrated execution in this tournament and we have no counter-evidence from B8. However, the lack of B8 data prevents confidence above ~30% in either direction. REVERSAL RISK FOR IMMINENT LIVE EVENT: With ~5 hours until match start, any reversal would require either B8 to demonstrate unexpected strong form OR Inner Circle to choke on known maps. The 2-0 result over FaZe is already priced in; no major new information is likely to emerge. This supports the current market being roughly fair, not a major misprice. CONCLUSION: Assign slight edge to Inner Circle based on demonstrated tournament form (2-0 win), but recognize this probability is highly uncertain due to complete absence of B8 performance data. Do not increase confidence scores; the data simply does not support high conviction in either direction.", "key_factor": "In competitive Counter-Strike BO3 matches between similarly-ranked teams at major tournaments, the outcome is approximately 50-50 absent strong individual player form data or recent head-to-head records. Teams with demonstrated tournament wins (e.g., 2-0 over ranked opponents) win their next group stage match ~55-60% of the time; teams with unknown or inconsistent form win ~40-45%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market is priced nearly at 50-50 (45/55), reflecting genuine uncertainty due to extreme data asymmetry \u2014 Inner Circle has ONE verifiable result (2-0 over FaZe), while B8 has zero tournament performance data in briefing. Inner Circle's win over FaZe appears artificially inflated in market psychology \u2014 FaZe's 0-3 record signals tournament-wide competitive collapse, not Inner Circle's dominance. Beating a faltering team is weak evidence for BO3 strength. B8 is a data void: no results, no form indicators, no head-to-head history provided. Market may be unconsciously anchoring on the ONLY positive signal (Inner Circle beat FaZe), creating false confidence in NO side despite equivalent ignorance about B8's actual capability. Crowd is underweighting the BO3 format risk \u2014 requires 2 map wins, high variance outcome. Single-match defeats (like FaZe 0-3) don't translate predictively to multi-map series. 45% YES pricing suggests slight crowd lean toward Inner Circle, but this lean is built on sand: one win vs. a struggling team. If B8 is a respectable mid-tier team, market has mispri\u00adced risk on both sides equally. With ~5 hours to match start, reversal probability is extremely low; market will likely converge to 35-65 or 65-35 shortly before match begins based on betting volume and late-arriving roster/form information. Confidence scores depressed symmetrically (35/38) because briefing provides insufficient data to confidently evaluate either team's actual strength \u2014 this is a coin flip disguised as a 45/55 market.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Inner Circle demonstrated concrete tournament form by defeating FaZe 2-0, but FaZe's 0-3 record indicates FaZe is performing significantly below their usual standard this event\u2014this may reflect FaZe collapse rather than Inner Circle excellence. B8's performance at PGL Bucharest is completely absent from briefing; no wins, losses, map records, or player form data available for direct comparison. BO3 format (first-to-2-maps) is inherently less predictable than single-elim; map bans, veto phase, and specific map pool matchups can swing outcomes dramatically\u2014Inner Circle's 2-0 vs FaZe tells us little about B8 stylistic matchups. Market prices (YES 45% vs NO 55%) suggest slight underdog positioning for B8, but briefing provides insufficient asymmetric evidence to justify move beyond 50-50 baseline. Both teams appear to be in mid-pack competitive tier at this tournament (Inner Circle in 0-2 pool post day-two alongside s1mple/Voca); no Tier-1 seeding or dominant form indicators present. Critical data gap: B8's recent LAN results, current roster stability, map win rates, and head-to-head record vs Inner Circle entirely missing from briefing. Event timing (TODAY, ~5 hours to match start) means minimal new information will arrive; market should reflect existing uncertainty unless late roster/coach statements emerge. High volume ($583k) suggests market is liquid but not necessarily efficient\u2014esports markets often misprice when team-specific form data is asymmetrically distributed among bettors.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle's 2-0 over FaZe is a single data point in a volatile BO3 format where map pool matchups, individual player performance variance, and tactical preparation carry equal or greater weight than head-to-head seeding."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Inner Circle's 2-0 over FaZe is being over-weighted: FaZe's 0-3 record signals systemic collapse, not necessarily that Inner Circle is tier-1. Beating a broken FaZe is a weak credential. B8's complete absence from the briefing is a red flag for both sides: no stats means no evidence of underperformance, but also no evidence of competitiveness. BO3 is highly format-dependent. Market pricing at 45/55 suggests near coin-flip confidence; this reflects genuine information parity, not a clear edge to Inner Circle. The $583k volume indicates sharp money is split. Black swan #1: B8 may have studied Inner Circle's map veto patterns and anti-stratted them for this specific match. CS:GO/CS2 map meta shifts fast; one new utility setup or execute can flip a series. Black swan #2: Inner Circle's win over FaZe may have created a false confidence/complacency effect in their mental model going into B8. Upset wins in group stages sometimes precede letdowns. Black swan #3: Personnel/roster fluidity not mentioned in briefing. If either team has a stand-in, illness, or last-minute sub, BO3 execution suffers disproportionately. Timing constraint: EVENT IS TODAY, 5 hours to match. No time for line movement based on late roster news; if a key player is benched or subbed, market will not adjust before tipoff. Neither team has strong global ranking signals in briefing (only regional noise, MIBR/FaZe/s1mple commentary). This is a mid-tier regional/CIS-adjacent matchup, not a marquee clash. Upsets are more frequent in these tiers. Inner Circle listed in '0-2 pool' post-day-two suggests they may have already dropped 2 matches before the FaZe win. Comeback wins in group stages are volatile; next match often reverts to mean. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH confidence in YES (B8 wins) is only 45 because B8 is invisible; confidence in NO is only 38 because Inner Circle's credential (FaZe) is weak and they were 0-2 before the 2-0 run.", "key_factor": "B8 deploys a recently-patched anti-eco or map-control meta that specifically counters Inner Circle's map pool strengths, or Inner Circle's morale collapses after a surprise loss to a lower-seeded team in warm-up/scrim."}], "final_score": 0.44943462897526504, "no_score": 0.5395092024539878, "edge": -0.000565371024734973, "no_edge": -0.010490797546012232, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for NO (need \u226560%); NO-side confidence too low: 41% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1896662", "question": "Counter-Strike: B8 vs Inner Circle Esports (BO3) - PGL Bucharest Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 4 match between B8 and Inner Circle Esports in the PGL Bucharest Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"B8\" if B8 win the match against Inner Circle Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle Esports\" if Inner Circle Esports win the match against B8.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:05:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:05:00Z", "yes_price": 0.45, "volume_usd": 583932.716461, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Complete overview of PGL Bucharest 2026 here.", "See prize distribution, attending teams, brackets and much more!", "FaZe's misery continues as they exit the Romanian tournament with a 0-3 record.", "karrigan gave HLTV his frank assessment of FaZe's disastrous season, as well as an inner look at the emotions him and his team are going through.", "Get the complete overview of 3DMAX's current lineup, upcoming matches, recent results and much more.", "By Nohte \u00b7 Short: 1win take the trophy at MPKBK CIS LAN S4.", "World ranking HLTV regional ranking Regional rankings Global Valve ranking Valve ranking Global Valve Regional ranking Regional Valve ranking Global Valve", "MIBR recently followed in FURIA's footsteps, bringing in players from the European scene to supplement their Brazilian lineup.", "\"There are some wild dreams that at our best, in good form, we could play around the top 10,\" El1an said.", "s1mple and company are joined by FaZe, Inner Circle, and Voca in the 0-2 pool."], "news_summary": "B8 and Inner Circle Esports are set to meet in a BO3 at PGL Bucharest 2026 Group Stage. Inner Circle demonstrated competitive strength by defeating FaZe 2-0 in the tournament, while FaZe exited with a 0-3 record, indicating FaZe's poor performance at the event. BC.Game and FaZe were mentioned as being in the 0-2 pool after day two, suggesting the tournament had multiple teams struggling early. Limited specific information is available about B8's current form or performance at PGL Bucharest.", "side_yes_case": ["Inner Circle defeated FaZe 2-0, demonstrating tournament-level competitive capability", "FaZe's 0-3 elimination record suggests the tournament features significant competitive variation", "Inner Circle advancing past early rounds indicates superior group stage performance versus eliminated teams"], "side_no_case": ["B8's specific performance and form at PGL Bucharest is not detailed in search results", "Limited direct comparison data between B8 and Inner Circle available", "BO3 format favors consistency; outcome depends heavily on which team executes better across multiple maps"], "key_context": ["PGL Bucharest 2026 Group Stage - ongoing tournament with multiple teams in elimination pool", "Inner Circle's 2-0 victory over FaZe occurred within same tournament, providing recent form data point", "BO3 format requires winning 2 maps, not a single elimination match", "FaZe's season-long struggles noted by karrigan; tournament context shows competitive disparity exists"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T09:45:48.522897Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T15:05:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T13:11:09.353666+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "2ceb8fa9-4291-41b7-a152-0fe36d94de64", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T09:47:32.461652+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1855337", "question": "Valorant: FunPlus Phoenix vs TYLOO (BO3) - VCT China Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FunPlus Phoenix and TYLOO in the VCT China Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FunPlus Phoenix\" if FunPlus Phoenix win the match against TYLOO.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TYLOO\" if TYLOO win the match against FunPlus Phoenix.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.23, "volume_usd": 65909.56925699995, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.25, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.7, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: YES = FunPlus Phoenix wins the BO3 match against TYLOO on April 7, 2026. EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for April 7 at 5:00 AM ET (10:00 AM UTC). Briefing timestamp is 09:47 UTC on April 7, meaning match start is imminent or already underway. CURRENT MARKET PRICING: YES at 23%, NO at 77% \u2014 market assigns strong probability to TYLOO victory, consistent with TYLOO's 2-0 record and +11 map differential. TYLOO STRENGTHS: Undefeated 2-0 record in group play; 4-1 map record; +11 map differential (best in group); defeated Bilibili Gaming 2-1 showing ability to beat quality opponents; leads Group Alpha standings. FUNPLUS PHOENIX WEAKNESSES: 1-1 record; recently lost to JD Gaming 1-2 (March 31); inconsistent form despite 3-2 map record and +10 differential; sits 4th in standings, one loss behind TYLOO. FUNPLUS PHOENIX STRENGTHS: Only 1 map differential behind TYLOO (+10 vs +11); defeated All Gamers 2-0 cleanly; map record very close (3-2 vs 4-1); competitive capability demonstrated. COMPETITIVE CONTEXT: Both teams closely matched in map performance; only separated by one win and one map differential point. This is not a mismatch. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: Market at 23% YES implies ~77% confidence in TYLOO. This appears reasonable given TYLOO's undefeated status and head-to-head standing advantage, though the narrow map differential and closeness of records suggest YES at 25-30% is defensible. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (70) because TYLOO's objective record is superior and market agreement is strong. Lower confidence in YES (35) because while FunPlus has legitimate competitive metrics, the briefing lacks team form trends, recent scrims, or meta advantages that would justify higher probability for upset. NO MECHANISM RISK IDENTIFIED: Resolution criteria are clear; team names are unambiguous; VLR.gg tracking is standard source; no forfeit/walkover risk apparent. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: TYLOO favored at 75%, FunPlus Phoenix at 25%. Market price of 23% YES aligns closely; slight adjustment to 25% acknowledges the competitive closeness while respecting TYLOO's objective standings advantage.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE with ~5 hours to resolution; briefing data is current as of 09:47 UTC on event day, so outcome is likely already determined or nearly so, making real-time data the primary factor."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "TYLOO is the clear favorite: 2-0 record vs FunPlus Phoenix's 1-1 record; TYLOO leads Group Alpha standings decisively. TYLOO's map record (4-1, +11 differential) is superior to FunPlus Phoenix (3-2, +10 differential), indicating more consistent dominance across multiple games in the group stage. Direct competition evidence favors TYLOO: they defeated Bilibili Gaming 2-1 in Week 1, a team that FunPlus has not yet faced, demonstrating capacity to beat tier-1 opposition. FunPlus Phoenix shows inconsistency: despite starting strong with a 2-0 Week 1 win vs All Gamers, they dropped to 1-1 after a 1-2 loss to JD Gaming, raising reliability questions. Underdog FunPlus advantages are marginal: their map differential (+10) is only 1 point behind TYLOO (+11), and both teams remain relatively close in aggregate competition level. Pressure dynamics favor FunPlus slightly: TYLOO's undefeated record creates psychological burden going into this match; FunPlus plays with less expectation weight. However, FunPlus must overcome form volatility: their 1-1 current record after an early loss suggests inconsistency that TYLOO's 2-0 perfect start does not exhibit. Both teams are competitive mid-tier in the group with no dominant outliers, meaning the 2-0 vs 1-1 record gap is the strongest differentiator available. Market pricing at 77% NO (23% YES) is reasonable given TYLOO's superior record and map record, though FunPlus is not dramatically outmatched\u2014confidence in NO side is moderately high but not overwhelming. Event timing TODAY with ~5 hours to match resolution limits ability for unexpected roster changes or major news shifts; current form and standings are the primary drivers.", "key_factor": "TYLOO's perfect 2-0 record with superior map differential (+11 vs +10) and demonstrated ability to beat strong opponents like Bilibili Gaming positions them as the stronger favorite in this head-to-head matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES (FunPlus) priced at 23% is heavily favored toward NO (TYLOO at 77%), making FunPlus the clear underdog despite competitive standings. TYLOO'S FRAGILITY: Undefeated record (2-0) creates vulnerability\u2014pressure mounts in Week 2 when stakes intensify; teams with perfect records often falter when directly challenged by competitive peers. MAP DIFFERENTIAL PARITY: FunPlus achieved +10 differential with only 1 win (3-2 record), while TYLOO achieved +11 with 2 wins (4-1 record). FunPlus's efficiency suggests closer competitive reality than win-loss suggests\u2014this narrow margin indicates TYLOO's dominance may be overstated. FunPlus MOMENTUM: FunPlus cleanly beat All Gamers 2-0 in Week 1, demonstrating clean victory capability; recent loss to JD Gaming (1-2) was competitive, not a blowout, suggesting form stabilization rather than decline. STANDINGS VOLATILITY: The briefing shows six teams in close competition; no team has dominant separation. One-win margin between 1st and 4th place indicates high-parity environment where upsets are structurally common. PSYCHOLOGICAL DYNAMICS: FunPlus plays with lower expectation pressure as underdog; TYLOO's 2-0 status and top-seed mentality may breed complacency or tactical predictability that FunPlus can exploit. DIRECT MATCHUP UNKNOWN: No prior head-to-head data provided between these teams in briefing; this removes betting-market advantage for TYLOO\u2014FunPlus is not a proven underdog matchup-wise, just standings-wise. BOX SCORE EFFICIENCY: FunPlus's +10 differential per win is nearly identical to TYLOO's (+11 per 2 wins). This suggests teams are functionally closer in competitive strength than 2-0 vs 1-1 framing implies. RISK TO NO NARRATIVE: Market prices assume TYLOO's undefeated status translates to match victory with 77% confidence\u2014assumes standings predict outcomes linearly, which VCT history refutes in group-stage volatility. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES underdog case (42) reflects map differential and parity data; lower confidence in NO (65) reflects TYLOO's real standout performance but acknowledges lack of direct matchup history and inherent playoff-style volatility.", "key_factor": "FunPlus Phoenix's superior map differential efficiency (+10 vs +11 with one fewer win) suggests closer competitive equilibrium than standings indicate, combined with psychological advantage of being underdog in high-pressure Week 2 match."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "TYLOO is the statistical favorite: 2-0 record vs FunPlus Phoenix's 1-1, leading Group Alpha standings by one win. Map differential strongly favors TYLOO: +11 versus FunPlus Phoenix's +10\u2014narrow margin but TYLOO has demonstrated more consistent map-level execution. TYLOO showed pedigree by defeating Bilibili Gaming 2-1 in Week 1, indicating ability to close out competitive BO3 matches against strong opponents. FunPlus Phoenix's 1-1 record with a 1-2 loss to JD Gaming suggests inconsistency in high-pressure situations; however, their 2-0 cleanup of All Gamers shows capability when form clicks. The market prices YES (FunPlus) at 23% and NO (TYLOO) at 77%. Historical precedent suggests a 2-0 team versus a 1-1 team in esports group play typically trades closer to 60-65% for the favored side, making the 77% price moderately aggressive but defensible. Esports volatility is high: individual player performance, draft execution, and momentum shifts can overcome seeding. FunPlus plays as underdog with less pressure; TYLOO's undefeated status carries psychological weight. Confidence in YES is moderate (45): FunPlus has shown capability but lacks the win-record foundation; data gap on head-to-head history and recent form volatility. Confidence in NO is higher (62): TYLOO's 2-0 start, superior map record, and demonstrated wins against strong teams provide clearer evidence; however, inherent esports unpredictability and the possibility of a FunPlus hot streak prevent very high confidence. Event timing (TODAY, ~5 hours to start): Live/imminent matches have lower reversal probability, so the current market pricing is less subject to late swing. The 77% NO price is plausible given TYLOO's positioning. Base rate adjustment: Top-seeded (2-0) teams in BO3 group-stage matches historically win ~60-65%; the market at 77% NO implies ~23% YES, suggesting mild undervaluation of underdog probability but within reasonable bounds for a volatile esport.", "key_factor": "In esports best-of-3 group-stage matches between evenly-matched teams (within 1-2 wins and <5 map differential), the higher-seeded team wins ~58-62% of the time; underdog teams in similar scenarios win ~38-42%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market is pricing TYLOO at 77% (NO) based on undefeated 2-0 record and superior map differential (+11 vs +10), creating a consensus fear trade favoring the leader. However, FunPlus Phoenix's near-identical map differential (+10 vs +11) and tighter point margin (54-44 vs 57-46) suggest far closer competitive parity than the 23% YES price reflects. TYLOO's undefeated status carries psychological weight in the market; teams under 'must-not-lose' pressure often underperform in BO3 formats where momentum shifts are critical. FunPlus Phoenix's 1-1 record masks competitive consistency \u2014 they cleanly beat All Gamers 2-0 (Week 1) and only narrowly lost to JD Gaming 1-2, suggesting volatile matchup outcomes rather than true weakness. Market is exhibiting FEAR-driven overpricing of TYLOO's 2-0 record without properly discounting: (1) the marginal gap in standings, (2) BO3 volatility favoring underdogs, (3) TYLOO's mental pressure as undefeated. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (5 hours to resolution); reversal requires match to occur, but briefing shows match scheduled and both teams prepared. No cancellation or forfeiture signals present. Confidence in YES (72%) driven by strong structural underpricing relative to map parity; confidence in NO (45%) reflects uncertainty around TYLOO's mental state under pressure and BO3 volatility \u2014 insufficient public data on team morale/form changes. Fair probability should reflect: TYLOO favored (~60-65%) on record, but FunPlus Phoenix's 35-40% equity is being suppressed to 23% by crowd fear of the undefeated team. This is a rational apathy market: the briefing shows near-parity in execution metrics (maps, differential) but crowd has anchored on win-loss record alone, creating a potential value opportunity on FunPlus Phoenix at 23%.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "CASE FOR NO (TYLOO favorite at 77% market price): TYLOO currently 2-0 with superior seeding, positive map differential (+11 vs +10), and demonstrated ability to win close matches (2-1 vs Bilibili Gaming), creating momentum and psychological advantage in direct matchup. MAP-LEVEL ANALYSIS FAVORS FUNPLUS: FunPlus Phoenix's +10 differential on 3-2 map record (60% win rate) outpaces TYLOO's 4-1 (80% rate only marginally better). The +1 differential gap (11 vs 10) is statistically noise given sample size; FunPlus may be the stronger unit on a per-map basis. HEAD-TO-HEAD VOLATILITY: Both teams face high-variance outcomes in BO3 format. FunPlus Phoenix's 1-2 loss to JD Gaming (stronger team in standings context) suggests they can be beaten; TYLOO has not faced a team of FunPlus caliber yet, raising uncertainty around how their 2-0 translates. PLAYOFF IMPLICATIONS REVERSE EXPECTATIONS: TYLOO at 2-0 faces elimination risk if they lose (drops to 2-1, vulnerable to tiebreaker scenarios). FunPlus at 1-1 plays with lower pressure\u2014a win moves them to 2-1, matching TYLOO and improving playoff odds. Psychological momentum favors the underdog. MARKET MISPRICING INDICATOR: NO side priced at 77% reflects raw standings recency bias. Market may be overweighting TYLOO's record without accounting for map-level parity and FunPlus's demonstrated tactical strength (clean 2-0 over All Gamers). VALORANT METAGAME VOLATILITY: Agent composition, patch version, and map pool can heavily favor one team's preparation. Briefing lacks agent/map veto data; tactical preparation unknown. BO3 allows teams to adapt between games\u2014FunPlus could exploit TYLOO's limited recent high-level opposition. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: High confidence in NO (65) due to TYLOO's clear standings lead and undefeated record creating structural advantage. Lower confidence in YES (42) because the underlying map-level data suggests closer match than 23% implies, but insufficient VOD/pick analysis to definitively claim FunPlus is favored\u2014market price may be anchoring to a reasonable baseline that coincidental form variance cannot fully invalidate. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~5 hours to start). Market has priced TYLOO heavily; large reversal unlikely absent significant new information (roster changes, withdrawal, technical issue). This reinforces modest probability for YES despite data suggesting tighter contest.", "key_factor": "TYLOO's 2-0 record masks vulnerability to map-level consistency (4-1 = 55.6% map win rate), while FunPlus Phoenix's 1-1 record with +10 differential (+54.5% map rate) suggests stronger underlying performance masked by one volatile match against JD Gaming (1-2 loss)."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "TYLOO's 2-0 record is inflated by context: they beat Bilibili Gaming (1-1 record) and Titan Esports Club (0-2, weakest team). FunPlus Phoenix's only loss was to JD Gaming (1-1), a comparably strong opponent \u2014 sample size and opponent quality are nearly equivalent. Map differential is nearly identical (+11 vs +10), suggesting performance quality is closer than win-loss records imply. TYLOO may be benefiting from a favorable early schedule rather than genuine superiority. FunPlus Phoenix has NO recent head-to-head data against TYLOO in the briefing; the match at 0-0 on Apr 07 is their first meeting. TYLOO's undefeated streak provides no direct evidence of dominance over FunPlus specifically. Absence of patch notes, meta analysis, or player roster changes in briefing creates a blind spot: if a recent Valorant patch or agent balance shift favors FunPlus's agent pool or tactical archetype, this could flip the match despite TYLOO's record. Psychological momentum cuts both ways: TYLOO's 2-0 record creates expectation and target-on-back pressure in a best-of-3 where a single upset map loss can cascade. FunPlus plays as underdog with nothing to lose. Market pricing at 23% YES / 77% NO is overcorrecting on win-loss record and not sufficiently weighting the near-parity in map differential, head-to-head uncertainty, and tactical variance inherent in competitive Valorant. FunPlus Phoenix's loss to JD Gaming 1-2 is early-week volatility, not a trend. Their 2-0 victory over All Gamers was clean, and they remain in contention for top-2 finish \u2014 motivation and preparation are high. BO3 format introduces variance: TYLOO's 4-1 map record means they've won 4 maps and lost 1 across 2 matches \u2014 a single upset in a best-of-3 could flip the series entirely if FunPlus secures 2 maps.", "key_factor": "FunPlus Phoenix executes a tactical or meta counter-pick strategy perfectly suited to this Week 2 meta shift, exploiting TYLOO's apparent reliance on the same playstyle that worked in Week 1 against weaker opposition."}], "final_score": 0.36390625, "no_score": 0.6748336594911937, "edge": 0.13390624999999998, "no_edge": -0.09516634050880635, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 63% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1855337", "question": "Valorant: FunPlus Phoenix vs TYLOO (BO3) - VCT China Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between FunPlus Phoenix and TYLOO in the VCT China Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 7 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FunPlus Phoenix\" if FunPlus Phoenix win the match against TYLOO.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TYLOO\" if TYLOO win the match against FunPlus Phoenix.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T15:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T09:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.23, "volume_usd": 65909.56925699995, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["TYLOO\nBilibili Gaming\nJD Gaming\nFunPlus Phoenix\nAll Gamers\nTitan Esports Club\nTYLOO\nBilibili Gaming\nJD Gaming\nFunPlus Phoenix\nAll Gamers\nTitan Esports Club [...] |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| All Gamers |  | 0-0 Apr 15 | 0-0 Apr 11 | 0-0 Apr 09 | 2-1 Mar 31 | 0-2 Apr 03 |\n| Bilibili Gaming | 0-0 Apr 15 |  | 1-2 Apr 02 | 2-0 Apr 05 | 0-0 Apr 07 | 0-0 Apr 10 |\n| TYLOO | 0-0 Apr 11 | 2-1 Apr 02 |  | 0-0 Apr 14 | 2-0 Apr 04 | 0-0 Apr 07 |\n| JD Gaming | 0-0 Apr 09 | 0-2 Apr 05 | 0-0 Apr 14 |  | 0-0 Apr 12 | 2-1 Apr 01 |\n| Titan Esports Club | 1-2 Mar 31 | 0-0 Apr 07 | 0-2 Apr 04 | 0-0 Apr 12 |  | 0-0 Apr 15 |\n| FunPlus Phoenix | 2-0 Apr 03 | 0-0 Apr 10 | 0-0 Apr 07 | 1-2 Apr 01 | 0-0 Apr 15 |  |\n|  | All Gamers | Bilibili Gaming | TYLOO | JD Gaming | Titan Esports Club | F