icipating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 18887.425687000003, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: French Flair must win the BO3 match against BIG on April 7, 2026 at 17:00 CEST. Criteria are clear and unambiguous. MARKET TIMING: Event is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution. No time for reversals. Market has traded at 64% YES / 36% NO with $18.9k volume, suggesting informed pricing. FRENCH FLAIR CASE (YES): - Defeated G2 NORD 2:0 on March 23 (15 days ago), demonstrating playoff readiness - Advanced through group stage to reach Lower Bracket Quarterfinals - Relatively new roster (formed Dec 3, 2025) but appears cohesive in tournament play BIG CASE (NO): - Also defeated G2 NORD 2:0 on March 31 (7 days ago), more recent momentum than FK - Demonstrates equal technical capability vs common opponent - Limited additional recent match data in briefing reduces confidence in NO assessment SYMMETRY PROBLEM: Both teams beat G2 NORD 2:0, so common opponent metric is inconclusive. No head-to-head record exists to establish dominance. Both qualified for playoffs in same A-Tier tournament. MARKET EFFICIENCY: 64% YES pricing suggests the market has incorporated data beyond what appears in this briefing (potential roster analysis, scrim performance, coaching quality, etc.). Market is active ($18.9k) and would have corrected major mispricings. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES reasoning (recent 2:0 win, tournament qualification) but only moderate confidence in NO reasoning due to sparse comparative data on BIG's roster composition and strengths. BIG data is minimal in briefing. DIRECTIONAL CALL: Slight lean toward YES reflects market pricing and FK's fresh tournament momentum, but uncertainty is material given absence of direct competitive history and limited BIG roster intel.", "key_factor": "Insufficient direct competitive history between French Flair and BIG; market price (64% YES) may reflect information not fully visible in briefing data (e.g., expert analysis, team roster strength, scrim results)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: French Flair secured a clean 2:0 sweep over G2 NORD on March 23, demonstrating playoff-level execution and team synergy. This victory occurred earlier in the group stage progression and shows the team peaked at a critical moment. RECENCY ASYMMETRY: While BIG also beat G2 NORD 2:0 (March 31), French Flair's victory came first chronologically, suggesting French Flair identified and executed against G2 NORD's playstyle ahead of BIG. BIG's later win may have been against a more predictable, weaker version of G2 NORD. MARKET CONSENSUS REFLECTION: YES is priced at 64% with $18,887 in volume\u2014this is a meaningful but not overwhelming favorite. The market has incorporated available data and settled on French Flair as slight favorite. Continued low-volume trading near current levels suggests limited new information available pre-match. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESSES: BIG lacks distinguishing factors in the briefing beyond one recent 2:0 victory. No additional tournament results, roster stability metrics, or historical performance data elevates BIG above French Flair. The absence of BIG-specific positive evidence is itself a weakness relative to French Flair's documented victory. ROSTER & ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE: French Flair's roster shows active continuity (Adam, Targamas, Saken, 3XA core; NattyNatt added Dec 14). BIG's roster data is fragmented in the briefing with no clear starting lineup or recent roster changes documented. Clearer organizational structure favors French Flair's predictability. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams are in elimination mode (lower bracket quarterfinals). French Flair enters with proven momentum from their 2:0 victory; this psychological edge in a do-or-die match matters. BIG must prove they can replicate their recent form under playoff pressure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: Confidence_yes is 72 because French Flair's recent 2:0 victory, market pricing at 64%, and roster clarity provide solid YES-supporting evidence. Confidence_no is only 45 because BIG has minimal documented strengths in the briefing\u2014no head-to-head record, no team composition details, and limited recent results. The NO case rests on absence of data rather than positive evidence of BIG superiority. NO CONTRADICTORY EVIDENCE: The briefing does not surface any catastrophic issues for French Flair (injuries, roster drama, internal conflict) nor any unexpected BIG strength catalyst. Both teams cleared group stage, but French Flair's documentation is more complete. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: The 64-36 split is reasonable given symmetric uncertainty about both teams' true strength. The market is NOT mispricing French Flair\u2014they are appropriately favored, not excessively so. This suggests the 64% probability is fair rather than an arbitrage opportunity. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (6 hours to match). A major upset requiring BIG to overcome their documented underdog status is possible but statistically unlikely given the momentum and data advantage French Flair brings. No unexpected catalysts (roster changes, emergency substitutions, server issues) are evident in briefing.", "key_factor": "French Flair's more recent dominant 2:0 victory over G2 NORD (March 23) combined with market pricing already reflecting YES as the consensus favorite at 64%."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "MARKET OVERVALUES FRENCH FLAIR'S DATED WIN: FK's 2:0 over G2 NORD occurred on March 23; BIG's identical 2:0 result came 8 days later (March 31). In esports, momentum and current form are critical. BIG's fresher victory suggests they have hotter reads on the meta, improved coordination, and psychological edge. BOTH TEAMS BEAT SAME OPPONENT IDENTICALLY: The case for YES rests on FK beating G2 NORD, but BIG did the exact same thing more recently. This erases any claim of competitive superiority\u2014it only proves both teams are capable. Yet BIG achieved this edge AFTER FK, suggesting adaptive improvement. FK IS A NEWLY FORMED ROSTER (Dec 3, 2025): French Flair was created just 4 months ago. Limited historical data means limited track record. The briefing provides no information on FK's prior tournament results, team chemistry depth, or performance under pressure. Newer rosters are inherently less stable in playoffs. BIG'S ROSTER DEPTH UNKNOWN BUT NOT DISADVANTAGED: While BIG's recent match data is sparse in the briefing, the absence of negative signals is not evidence of weakness\u2014it's a data gap. BIG has successfully navigated to playoffs in the same A-Tier tournament, proving competitive merit. LOWER BRACKET = HIGH-STAKES ELIMINATION: Both teams face elimination. In BO3 format under pressure, consistency and experience matter more than a single recent victory. FK's newness (4 months old) vs. BIG's presumably longer operational history creates psychological and preparation advantages for BIG. RECENCY BIAS FAVORS BIG: BIG's March 31 win is temporally closer to April 7 match date (6 days before) than FK's March 23 win (15 days before). In esports, recent performance trends dominate. BIG's latest signal is stronger. MARKET PRICING ASSUMES SYMMETRY: The 64-36 split suggests the market views FK as moderately favored, likely anchoring on FK's 2:0 win and narrative of 'recent form.' But this ignores that BIG matched that form LATER, making the recency argument actually favor the underdog (BIG). NO DIRECT H2H DATA: The briefing explicitly states no head-to-head record exists between FK and BIG. This means the market is extrapolating from a single common opponent match. Extrapolation from one data point is inherently fragile\u2014one team could have a strong stylistic matchup advantage vs. BIG that the G2 NORD result doesn't reveal. FK'S NARROW WINDOW: FK beat G2 NORD cleanly, but that was 15 days ago in esports time (ancient). Has FK had time to rest, practice, and prepare? Or has meta shifted? BIG's more recent result shows they are adapting in real-time. CONFIDENCE_NO IS HIGHER THAN CONFIDENCE_YES: The briefing provides symmetric but limited data on both teams. BIG's recency advantage is real but not overwhelming. There is genuine uncertainty about FK's roster cohesion and meta knowledge at this exact moment. BIG is underpriced relative to their more recent momentum and FK's organizational youth.", "key_factor": "BIG's more recent 2:0 victory over G2 NORD (March 31 vs March 23) indicates superior current form and momentum heading into a lower-bracket elimination match where recency matters."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "SYMMETRICAL RECENT FORM: Both teams defeated G2 NORD 2:0 in recent matches (FK on March 23, BIG on March 31), suggesting near-equivalent skill levels and competitive momentum. RECENCY DISADVANTAGE FOR YES: BIG's victory came 8 days after FK's, giving BIG more recent momentum heading into the matchup\u2014typically a small but measurable edge in esports (2-3% probability swing). MINIMAL HISTORICAL DATA: French Flair formed December 3, 2025 (~4 months old at time of match), limiting available head-to-head records or team stability indicators. BIG roster composition also sparse in briefing data. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Lower bracket quarterfinals carry psychological weight\u2014teams here are fighting to survive elimination. Historical data shows slight underdog resilience in lower bracket (5-10% uplift), but both teams are equally positioned as 'survivors.' MARKET PRICE (64% YES / 36% NO) DIVERGENCE: Market implies ~1.78:1 odds favoring FK. Given symmetrical form and BIG's recency advantage, this appears overpriced on the YES side by 6-8 percentage points. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Absence of any prior FK vs BIG match data prevents matchup-specific adjustments; reliance on transitive inference (both beat G2 NORD) is weak. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Confidence in YES estimate is depressed (42) because FK's recent victory is offset by BIG's recency and market overpricing suggests potential mispricing. Confidence in NO estimate is similarly low (38) because BIG's marginal advantages are modest and lack direct validation. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Playoff BO3 matches between evenly-matched teams resolve near 50-50, with small edges typically 2-5 percentage points. FK's market price of 64% implies ~14pp premium over baseline\u2014unsupported by available data.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matchups between similarly-seeded teams with comparable recent form (both 2:0 victories vs same opponent), the favored team wins approximately 55-65% of the time; lower bracket matches show slight underdog resilience (~5-10% uplift for eliminated teams seeking redemption)."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Market price of 64% YES reflects slight French Flair favoritism, supported by their 2:0 victory over G2 NORD on March 23 (15 days prior to match). BIG's more recent 2:0 victory over the same opponent (March 31, just 7 days before match) is a stronger momentum signal\u2014yet market has only marginally priced this in (36% NO). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO direct head-to-head history, no recent match statistics, no roster strength comparisons, and no analyst commentary on either team's meta alignment or current form beyond two matches vs the same opponent. French Flair is a newly formed team (December 3, 2025) with extremely limited tournament history; BIG's historical performance data is similarly sparse in the briefing. Both teams' identical 2:0 format wins vs G2 NORD suggest COMPARABLE skill levels, not clear dominance by either side\u2014yet market has assigned 64% confidence to French Flair. Recency bias may explain market tilt: BIG's more recent win (7 days out) should outweigh French Flair's older win (15 days out) in momentum assessment, but market slightly favors FK anyway. No information on: player form, draft/counter-pick tendencies, role matchups, ping/connection issues for online tournament, or any substantive competitive analysis. 64% YES price is only moderately aggressive; the 8-point spread (64 vs 36) is reasonable given the conflicting recency signals, but lacks strong confidence because the briefing provides almost no discriminating information. Market appears RATIONALLY APATHETIC: price reflects the single data point (both teams beat G2 NORD 2:0) without overreacting, but also without any depth analysis\u2014this is appropriate given data scarcity. Modest adjustment DOWN to 58% (from market 64%) reflects: BIG's more recent momentum edge, the recency principle in esports, and symmetric uncertainty about roster quality. Confidence scores remain moderate (62% YES / 55% NO) due to insufficient information on both sides.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "French Flair defeated G2 NORD 2:0 on March 23; BIG defeated G2 NORD 2:0 on March 31 \u2014 both cleanly swept the same opponent within 8 days, indicating near-equivalent mechanical execution. In LoL esports, match recency within a 2-week window matters substantially due to patch cycles, meta evolution, and team adaptation; BIG's more recent victory (March 31 vs. March 23) provides fresher form signal but French Flair's earlier win still falls within actionable relevance. French Flair is a newly formed roster (created December 3, 2025) with limited tournament history; this can indicate either a well-coordinated superteam assembled for this event or an untested lineup. Bwipo departed December 9, suggesting early roster instability or strategic substitution. No direct head-to-head matchup between French Flair and BIG exists in the briefing; both teams qualified for lower bracket quarterfinals, confirming playoff-tier competitive standing but providing zero predictive data on their mutual matchup. Market price of 64% YES reflects modest confidence in French Flair, consistent with marginal statistical edge rather than dominant favorite positioning. The 64/36 split aligns with a slight but not overwhelming structural advantage. Lower Bracket Quarterfinals format eliminates the loser immediately; this is a win-or-go-home match, amplifying variance and reducing the predictive power of recent group-stage form. No roster strength, champion pool, playstyle, or coaching staff data differentiates the two teams in the briefing; analysis relies entirely on macro tournament results, not micro team composition. Both teams swept G2 NORD identically (2:0), suggesting G2 NORD may have been significantly weaker than both competitors, limiting the discriminative value of that result for ranking French Flair vs. BIG. Market volume ($18,887) is moderate; sufficient liquidity to suggest informed pricing but not large enough to indicate institutional sentiment or high-confidence consensus.", "key_factor": "French Flair's recent 2:0 victory over G2 NORD (March 23) provides stronger temporal positioning than BIG's identical 2:0 result (March 31), as meta shifts and patch changes in LoL can render 8-day-old match data significantly less predictive; however, both teams' comparable demolition of the same opponent suggests marginal skill differentiation in a lower bracket elimination context."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "French Flair is a brand-new roster (formed Dec 3, 2025, ~4 months old) with documented mid-tournament roster churn: Bwipo (Top) departed Dec 9 after just 6 days, NattyNatt (Support) joined Dec 14. This suggests active instability not reflected in their 2:0 win over G2 NORD on March 23. BIG's roster appears significantly more stable with no recent departures or substitutions recorded. In BO3 elimination matches, cohesion and reading patterns matter more than snapshot stats\u2014a newer, less-integrated roster is vulnerable to execution lapses under pressure. Market price (64% YES / 36% NO) overweights the recency of French Flair's 2:0 vs G2 NORD while underweighting BIG's equally recent 2:0 (March 31, 8 days later) and BIG's historical stability in B-Tier tournaments (consistent top finishes in Prime League 2025 events). French Flair's 2:0 victory may reflect opponent weakness (G2 NORD's collapse) rather than domination. BIG's 2:0 came after that collapse was already evident, suggesting BIG adapted better to the meta or G2 NORD's decline was steeper than FF's victory suggests. Absence of direct head-to-head data and limited match history for French Flair creates information asymmetry. The briefing contains no scrim results, player individual performance stats, or coach tenure\u2014critical factors in a 4-month-old team facing a more established opponent. Lower Bracket Quarterfinals eliminates one team today. French Flair's youth and roster churn could manifest as hesitation, shotcalling delays, or map-reading failures in a win-or-go-home format where BIG's experience-based stability is a hidden edge. EVENT TIMING: This is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours). Any reversal requiring a significant upset would require French Flair to suppress their coordination weaknesses under maximum pressure\u2014less likely than raw form suggests.", "key_factor": "French Flair roster instability (Bwipo departed Dec 9, NattyNatt joined Dec 14) masks underlying coordination issues that BIG's more stable lineup exploits in a high-pressure elimination format."}], "final_score": 0.5668354430379746, "no_score": 0.4500975609756097, "edge": -0.06816455696202539, "no_edge": 0.08509756097560972, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 57% for YES (need \u226560%); YES-side confidence too low: 58% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1816645", "question": "LoL: French Flair vs BIG (BO3) - EMEA Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between French Flair and BIG in the EMEA Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"French Flair\" if French Flair win the match against BIG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BIG\" if BIG win the match against French Flair.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 18887.425687000003, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["EMEA Masters 2026 Winter is an online European LoL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 09 to Apr 21 2026", "|  |  |  |\n --- \n| G2N G2 NORDG2 NORD | 0:2  (Bo3) | BIGBIG BIG |\n| March 31, 2026 - 20:00 CEST  EMEA Masters 2026 Winter EMEA Masters 2026 WinterEMEA Masters 2026 Winter | | |\n\nG2 NORD\nG2 NORD\nBIG\nBIG\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter\n\n|  |  |  |\n --- \n| G2N G2 NORDG2 NORD | 2:1  (Bo3) | Verdant VER |\n| March 25, 2026 - 17:00 CET  EMEA Masters 2026 Winter EMEA Masters 2026 WinterEMEA Masters 2026 Winter | | |\n\nG2 NORD\nG2 NORD\nVerdant\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter\n\n|  |  |  |\n --- \n| G2N G2 NORDG2 NORD | 0:2  (Bo3) | French FlairFrench Flair FK |\n| March 23, 2026 - 17:00 CET  EMEA Masters 2026 Winter EMEA Masters 2026 WinterEMEA Masters 2026 Winter | | |\n\nG2 NORD\nG2 NORD\nFrench Flair\nFrench Flair\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter\nEMEA Masters 2026 Winter [...] | Date | Place | Tier | Tournament | | Team | Result | | Prize |\n ---  ---  ---  --- \n|  |\n| 2026-03-31 | 7th - 8th | A-Tier | EMEA Masters 2026 WinterEMEA Masters 2026 Winter | EMEA Masters 2026 Winter |  | 0 