{"run_id": "f75d3306-09d9-4db3-a2f2-a20e4a41b923", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T14:27:18.196555+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1903662", "question": "LoL: Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports vs Team Phantasma - Game 2 Winner", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports and Team Phantasma in the HLL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 7 at 9:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports\" if Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports win Game 2 against Team Phantasma.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Phantasma\" if Team Phantasma win Game 2 against Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports.\n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and Game 2 is concluded with a winner determined, this market will resolve based on the completed Game 2. \n\nIf Game 2 is not completed for any reason, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all) or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without play beginning, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T13:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.12, "volume_usd": 6195.472181999999, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.15, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO / TP WIN) DOMINANCE: Market prices TP at 88%, reflecting clear consensus. TP has won multiple documented Game 2s against GSMC in high-stakes tournaments (Summer Super Cup Finals, Season Finals), demonstrating consistent execution in this specific game state. TP'S GAME 2 EXECUTION: Search results explicitly show TP winning Game 2 in Summer Super Cup Finals 30:11 (crushing dominance), and TP reached both Finals tournaments, indicating sustained competitive superiority over GSMC in bo5 series contexts where Game 2 matters critically. SUPPORT DIFFERENTIAL WEAKNESS: GSMC's support REAVER shows structural vulnerabilities in Game 2 matchups\u2014KDA of 2.0-4.8 with 11-14 deaths. TP's support Centu counters this with elite 1.84 WPM (ward per minute), superior vision control and playmaking that controls mid-game tempo GSMC cannot match. VAYNEDETA ELITE BUT NOT SUFFICIENT: While Vaynedeta (GSMC ADC) maintains 9.9 KDA overall, individual excellence cannot overcome team-level deficiencies. TP has beaten GSMC despite Vaynedeta's presence\u2014suggesting macro coordination and support synergy matter more than solo carry potential. UNDERDOG (YES / GSMC) WEAKNESSES: GSMC relies on individual mechanical excellence (Peppe, Vaynedeta) but lacks the defensive infrastructure TP provides. Consistent support liability (REAVER deaths) in Game 2s creates pick/ban vulnerability and fight initiation disadvantage that TP exploits. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT AMBIGUITY CUTS BOTH WAYS: Multiple tournament instances in briefing create noise, but TP's documented Game 2 victories are EXPLICIT and RECENT, while GSMC's Game 2 wins lack corresponding tournament-stage evidence in same high-stakes context. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSIDERATION: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (~2.5 hours). For GSMC to win, they must overcome a 76-percentage-point deficit AND TP's established Game 2 playbook. No new catalysts or roster changes evident in briefing. This is not a mispricing correction scenario\u2014market reflects genuine head-to-head form. CONTRARIAN ANGLE WEAKNESS: GSMC advocates point to Vaynedeta KDA and GPM matching TP's bests. But tournament results\u2014the ultimate truth\u2014show TP winning the Finals Game 2 decisively. Statistics without wins are vanity metrics. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (78) because explicit Game 2 victories for TP are documented in tournament finals. Lower confidence in YES (35) because GSMC's Game 2 wins are not specifically documented in comparable finals contexts\u2014only individual stats, which have proven insufficient to beat TP's team execution.", "key_factor": "Team Phantasma's demonstrated ability to execute clean, decisive Game 2 victories against GSMC in tournament finals with strong support playmaking and vision control."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: 12% YES price indicates sharp confidence in TP winning Game 2; this extreme underdog pricing ($0.12/share) reflects either dominant recent form or significant skill gap perception. HISTORICAL DATA SHOWS SPLIT RESULTS: Briefing contains multiple TP vs GSMC Game 2 outcomes\u2014TP won one (30:11 stomp, Summer Super Cup Finals), GSMC won another (Season Finals). This suggests no overwhelming trend; teams are closer in capability than 88-12 pricing implies. GSMC INDIVIDUAL EXCELLENCE: Vaynedeta (9.9 KDA, 12.0-12.6 KDA in Game 2s), Peppe (6.2 KDA), and Manaty (7.8 KDA) rank among tournament's elite; GSMC achieved 2186 GPM matching TP's best performance. Statistical edge in mechanical skill. TP EXECUTION & CLEAN WINS: TP won Game 2 30:11 with dominant objective control; Centu's 1.84 WPM in that victory shows strong vision/playmaking. TP reached both Summer Super Cup Finals and Season Finals, demonstrating consistency. GSMC SUPPORT WEAKNESS CONCERN: REAVER's low KDA (2.0-4.8) and high deaths (11-14 in shown Game 2s) create defensive vulnerability that TP's aggression can exploit. Pallet/support matchup favors TP mechanically in skirmishes. GAME 2 CONTEXT: Game 2 in BO5 format carries draft strategy weight\u2014teams often pivot off Game 1 bans. Fearless Draft format (if applicable) increases champion diversity but both teams' historical adaptation is comparable. EXTREME UNDERDOG PRICING: 12% price is legitimate only if skill gap is massive or TP has overwhelming meta advantage. Briefing data does not support 88% certainty; evidence suggests ~25-35% true probability for GSMC based on head-to-head parity and player stats. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) because TP's tournament finals appearances, Game 2 victory precedent, and support stability are well-documented. Lower confidence in YES (35%) because GSMC's mechanical elite status is real but individual excellence does not guarantee team coordination under pressure in imminent match. IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Match resolves in ~2.5 hours with minimal time for reversal. If TP has prepared Game 2 specifically or won draft, 12% YES becomes 5-8%. If GSMC adapts from Game 1 loss, 12% should be 30-35%. Current price likely reflects TP having Game 1 advantage or momentum.", "key_factor": "In competitive LoL best-of-series, the underdog priced at 12% (~+700 implied odds) historically wins individual games at rates of 15-25% depending on skill gap magnitude and meta volatility. Game 2 outcomes in BO5s show slight patterns favoring teams that won Game 1, but individual game variance remains high (~25-30% upset rates even for heavy favorites)."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market is heavily skewed toward TP (88% NO), but briefing data shows GSMC won BOTH Game 2s in provided match records (30:11 and 39:42 victories visible in Season Finals data), contradicting current market consensus. Crowd psychology appears to be overweighting TP's overall finals appearances while ignoring the specific Game 2 win pattern favoring GSMC in the actual data presented. GSMC individual performance metrics dominate: Vaynedeta's 9.9 KDA, Peppe's 6.2 KDA rank top-tier; GSMC players appear in multiple 'most kills in single game' leaderboards, suggesting explosive game-winning potential in Game 2 specifically. TP's support player REAVER shows vulnerability in Game 2 contexts with 2.0-4.8 KDA and high death counts (11-14), contrasting sharply with GSMC's consistent execution. Market price (12% YES) severely undervalues GSMC given demonstrated Game 2 win rate in the briefing; suggests crowd panic or uninformed betting on TP brand rather than analytical Game 2 matchup data. Rational apathy risk: if market has not yet adjusted to live/imminent status (game starts in ~2.5 hours), the 88% NO price may still reflect stale historical perception rather than current roster/form. Confidence in YES is moderate (45) because briefing contains multiple tournament instances creating slight ambiguity about whether cited Game 2s correspond to THIS specific match; however evidence strongly favors GSMC in Game 2 format. Confidence in NO is moderate-high (62) because TP's Summer Finals Game 2 victory (30:11) is documented, and TP reached multiple finals, but the current 88% price appears overcorrected relative to GSMC's demonstrated Game 2 dominance in the data provided.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "TP won the documented Game 2s in both Summer Super Cup Finals (30:11) and Season Finals (39:42, 26:14) against GSMC with dominant execution and clean objective control. GSMC's support REAVER is the critical liability: 2.0-4.8 KDA with 11-14 deaths in Game 2 contexts, suggesting prone to early ganks and teamfight positioning errors that cascade into losses. TP's support Centu achieved 1.84 WPM (ward placement per minute) in the Summer Super Cup Game 2 win\u2014elite vision control indicating superior map awareness and proactive playmaking. GSMC's individual carry power (Vaynedeta 9.9 KDA, Peppe 6.2 KDA) is offset by support liability; LoL is a team game where one weak link (especially support) creates exploitable jungle/roam patterns. TP reached Season Finals and Summer Super Cup Finals, both best-of-five series where Game 2 winners (TP in both cases) often dictated series momentum through clean mid-game execution. Market pricing (88% NO, 12% YES) reflects the historical record in briefing: TP's 2-0 Game 2 record vs GSMC in documented finals creates asymmetric confidence. EVENT TIMING: Live/imminent (2.5 hours). Market has likely incorporated pre-game scrims and team form data; extreme price skew (12% YES) suggests institutional knowledge of GSMC's support vulnerability. Fearless Draft format reduces GSMC's adaptive flexibility if their Game 2 draft strategy relies on champion availability that counters TP\u2014TP's coaching staff appears well-prepared for GSMC's compositions. No contradictory data in briefing supports GSMC's Game 2 viability; all documented Game 2 outcomes favor TP in recent head-to-heads.", "key_factor": "Team Phantasma demonstrated superior Game 2 execution in both documented BO5 finals (Summer Super Cup 30:11 stomp, Season Finals consistent wins), while GSMC's support player (REAVER) consistently shows critical weaknesses in positioning/survivability (KDA 2.0-4.8, 11-14 deaths) that compound in high-pressure Game 2 scenarios where teams execute early game advantages."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "REAVER is a structural liability: across all Game 2 instances shown, REAVER's KDA ranges 2.0\u20134.8 with 11\u201314 deaths per game. This is the weakest link on GSMC's roster and creates compounding risk in a BO5 where momentum matters. TP's Centu demonstrated elite vision control (1.84 WPM) in their Game 2 victory, exploiting support weaknesses. If REAVER underperforms or is unavailable, GSMC loses their primary ward denial and engage setup. Tournament data shows TP won the Game 2 stomp 30:11 in Summer Super Cup Finals\u2014a decisive victory pattern that could repeat if GSMC's weak link is exposed or compromised. GSMC's offensive stars (Vaynedeta 9.9 KDA, Peppe 6.2 KDA) cannot compensate for a missing or tilted support in a game where coordinated teamfights and vision dominance determine mid-game windows. The briefing is silent on roster health, morale, or any recent personnel issues for either team\u2014a dangerous gap for a LIVE/IMMINENT event. Substitutions in college esports are more common and less coordinated than pro play. TP's overall tournament consistency (three finals appearances, strong GPM efficiency) suggests they have refined exploits against GSMC's specific macro weaknesses; a support replacement would amplify this. Market pricing (12% YES / 88% NO) reflects TP as heavy favorites, likely because GSMC's support deficiency is already priced in\u2014but unexpected unavailability of REAVER mid-series would push this to near 99% NO. GSMC won Game 2s in aggregate stats shown, but both victories featured REAVER's poor KDA, meaning GSMC is winning *despite* the support, not because of it\u2014a fragile scenario vulnerable to disruption.", "key_factor": "GSMC's support player REAVER suffers a disconnect or unexpected substitution mid-series, forcing a rookie or underperforming stand-in into a critical Game 2 where vision control and late-game positioning determine the outcome."}], "final_score": 0.1986486486486487, "no_score": 0.8091573033707866, "edge": 0.0786486486486487, "no_edge": -0.07084269662921339, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "CAUTIOUS", "pass_reason": "", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1903662", "question": "LoL: Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports vs Team Phantasma - Game 2 Winner", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports and Team Phantasma in the HLL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 7 at 9:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports\" if Gamespace Mediterranean College Esports win Game 2 a