S (UCAM) reflects slight edge based on evidence quality and form trajectory, but tempered by true uncertainty and lack of head-to-head data. This undercuts the market's 55% NO pricing\u2014UCAM appears slightly undervalued at 45%.", "key_factor": "UCAM's demonstrated dominance in Stage 3.1 playoffs (multiple 2-0 victories including against higher-tier opponents) combined with DNSTY's opaque match history and unproven playoff pedigree suggests the market undervalues UCAM's current form trajectory."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "UCAM shows stronger documented recent form: multiple 2-0 victories in Stage 3.1 (April 5 vs KPI), plus Stage 2 Playoffs win over Bar\u00e7a (March 7, 2-0). DNSTY also won 2-0 on April 5 (vs MT), but lacks detailed historical record in briefing to assess consistency or opponent quality. No direct head-to-head match history provided between UCAM and DNSTY, eliminating the strongest predictive signal. Both teams reach Upper Bracket Semifinal, indicating similar competitive standing; exact seeding/bracket position unknown from briefing. BO3 format mitigates single-match variance; both teams have demonstrated map-win capability recently. UCAM's documented wins include a top-tier opponent (Bar\u00e7a), suggesting higher ceiling than DNSTY's available data shows. Market price (45% YES / 55% NO) suggests slight NO lean; this is near-symmetric and reflects genuine uncertainty. Event timing is LIVE/IMMINENT (~5 hours to resolution): by this point, team lineups, meta shifts, and pre-match analysis are locked in; reversal probability is very low. Confidence asymmetry: stronger historical data on UCAM (confidence_yes = 48) vs. sparse data on DNSTY (confidence_no = 45) reflects briefing gaps equally on both sides. Probability slightly above 50 justified by UCAM's documented stronger recent opponent quality (Bar\u00e7a > MT), but margin is modest given lack of 