pecialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM shows consistent dominant performances: multiple consecutive 2-0 victories (vs KPI on April 5, vs Bar\u00e7a on March 7) indicate refined team coordination and meta adaptation during peak playoff timing. DNSTY's recent performance limited to single documented 2-0 win (vs MT on April 5); insufficient match history to assess consistency, map pool depth, or playoff pressure resilience. BO3 format favors teams with deeper strategic flexibility and proven map adaptability; UCAM's documented success across multiple opponents (KPI, Bar\u00e7a) suggests superior preparation. Bar\u00e7a eSports appearance in UCAM's recent wins is notable\u2014Bar\u00e7a competes in VCL EMEA tier, indicating UCAM has faced higher-tier competition than DNSTY's documented MT opponent. No direct head-to-head history between teams in briefing; market pricing (45% YES / 55% NO) reflects genuine uncertainty and data asymmetry favoring the underdog. Event timing is TODAY (~5 hours to resolution); extreme recency of April 5-7 matches means current roster and meta stability are confirmed, reducing tactical surprise factors. Playoff stage (Rising Phase 1 Playoffs vs regular season group play) typically features tighter map bans, less innovation, and higher correlation to raw team strength\u2014favors UCAM's demonstrated consistency. Confidence in YES is modest (62) due to sparse DNSTY data; confidence in NO is lower (48) because the briefing provides insufficient counter-evidence to justify overweighting DNSTY despite market pricing lean.", "key_factor": "UCAM's recent 2-0 victories in Stage 3.1 playoffs demonstrate superior current form and map control consistency, while DNSTY's single documented 2-0 win lacks sufficient recent match data to establish competitive parity in a high-pressure BO3 playoff context."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM's recent 2-0 victories (KPI, Bar\u00e7a) are against teams of unclear current standing; the briefing provides no comparative tier or recent form data for either opponent, making UCAM's 'strong form' claim unverifiable. DNSTY's single visible win (2-0 vs MT on April 5) is equally sparse in context; no information exists on MT's competitive level or meta adherence, so DNSTY's capability is assumed rather than proven. Head-to-head history is explicitly absent from the briefing\u2014zero direct UCAM vs DNSTY match records; both teams are near-peers in a B-Tier bracket with likely similar skill ceilings. BO3 format crucially favors adaptability and in-series adjustments over raw aggregate strength; a team that reads the meta faster or has superior tactical flexibility in map veto/agent selection can win 2-1 despite lower overall pedigree. Patch 12.05 is mentioned but no patch notes or agent/mechanic changes are described; if a recent patch heavily favors utility-heavy or aggressive sentinel plays (or vice versa), the team with deeper practice on that style gains a hidden edge. VCL EMEA Stage 1 results for UCAM show 0-2 losses and a 2-3 playoff loss, suggesting performance ceiling issues or fatigue; if UCAM has been grinding multiple tournaments in short span, mental fatigue or tactical staleness in playoffs is plausible. DNSTY appears to have less tournament volume in the briefing's match history, which could indicate either: (a) a newer roster that has trained intensively on a single meta, or (b) a team avoiding over-exposure and arriving fresh for playoffs. Absence of player-level data (injuries, stand-ins, role swaps, recent trades) is a critical blind spot; if UCAM's in-game leader or sentinel player is playing through an undisclosed issue, DNSTY's site execution could exploit it. Market prices (45% YES / 55% NO) reflect mild NO bias, suggesting smart money slightly favors DNSTY; this contrarian positioning is consistent with the theory that UCAM's recent wins are less impressive on closer scrutiny. Playoff intensity and pressure favor the team with sharper mental clarity; if DNSTY has genuinely lower expectations and UCAM is perceived favorite, psychological weight could shift defensive execution.", "key_factor": "DNSTY executes a meta-shift or map-pool strategy that exploits a specific weakness in UCAM's agent selection or site execution that recent stage matches did not fully expose."}], "final_score": 0.5105361930294906, "no_score": 0.4869189189189189, "edge": 0.06053619302949059, "no_edge": -0.06308108108108113, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 48% < 80% threshold", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1898498", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs DNSTY (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and DNSTY in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against DNSTY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DNSTY\" if DNSTY win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.45, "volume_usd": 27258.157460999995, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 Spain: Rising Stage 3 Phase 1 is an online Spanish VAL tournament organized by Riot Games and LVP.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "Game 2\n\nPatch 12.05\n\n### Match History\n\nHead to Head\n\n| Date | Tier | Tournament | Opponent | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| March 2, 2026 - 15:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 0 | KPI GamingKPI |  |\n| February 28, 2026 - 11:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 1 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| January 13, 2026 - 19:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 3 | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 1 : 1 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| October 10, 2025 - 18:00 CEST | Qualifier | RBHG: Spanish Qual.", "- Playoffs | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 1 : 2 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| July 13, 2025 - 18:00 CEST | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 3 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 0 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n\nUCAM EsportsUCAM [...] KPI GamingKPI\n\n| Date | Tournament | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  --- |\n| April 5, 2026 - 17:00 CEST | VCL Spain: Stage 3.1 | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n| March 2, 2026 - 15:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 0 : 2 | UCAM | Details |\n| March 1, 2026 - 13:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n| February 28, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 1 : 2 | UCAM | Details |\n| January 26, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 7 | 1 : 1 |  | Details |\n\nRetrieved from \"\"\n\nHidden categories:\n\n Pages with unknown player input in matches\n Matches\n Finished Matches [...] UCAM EsportsUCAM\n\n| Date | Tournament | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  --- |\n| March 28, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 2 : 3 |  | Details |\n| March 27, 2026 - 20:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 0 : 2 |  | Details |\n| March 26, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 2 : 1 | MDR | Details |\n| March 23, 2026 - 19:30 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group C | W : FF |  | Details |\n| March 22, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group C | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n\nKPI GamingKPI", "VCL Spain 2024: Split 2 - Round 12\n\nBar\u00e7a eSports\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| March 21, 2026 - 19:50 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B |  | 1 : 2 | FKS | Details |\n| March 19, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B |  | 0 : 2 | EP | Details |\n| March 8, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs |  | 3 : 1 | DSY | Details |\n| March 7, 2026 - 13:50 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs |  | 2 : 0 | UCAM | Details |\n| March 1, 2026 - 13:40 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B |  | 2 : 1 | NOVO | Details |\n\nVCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B\n\nVCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B [...] VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B\n\nFALKE ESPORTS\nFALKE ESPORTS\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| April 5, 2026 - 19:30 CEST | VCL Spain: Stage 3.1 | VCL Spain: Stage 3.1 |  | 2 : 0 | MT | Details |\n| March 1, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B |  | 0 : 2 | OTK | Details |\n| February 28, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B |  | 0 : 2 | NOVO | Details |\n| January 26, 2026 - 19:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 7 | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 7 |  | 0 : 2 | OTK | Details |\n| January 25, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 6 | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 6 |  | 0 : 2 | UCAM | Details |\n\nVCL Spain: Stage 3.1\n\nVCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B [...] | Date | Tier |  | Tournament | Opponent | Score | | | vs."], "news_summary": "UCAM Esports Club and DNSTY are competing in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs (BO3 format). UCAM has demonstrated strong recent form with multiple 2-0 victories in Stage 3.1, while DNSTY also secured a 2-0 win against MT on April 5, 2026. Both teams are competing in a B-Tier Spanish Valorant tournament organized by Riot Games and LVP. Head-to-head historical data between these specific teams is limited in the search results provided.", "side_yes_case": ["UCAM won 2-0 against KPI on April 5, 2026 in VCL Spain Stage 3.1, showing strong current form", "UCAM has consistent recent match history with multiple 2-0 victories in the playoff stage", "UCAM defeated Bar\u00e7a eSports 2-0 in Stage 2 Playoffs (March 7, 2026), proving ability to beat top-tier opponents"], "side_no_case": ["DNSTY secured a clean 2-0 victory against MT on April 5, 2026 in VCL Spain Stage 3.1", "Limited detailed match history for DNSTY makes performance assessment difficult, but recent playoff win demonstrates capability", "BO3 format allows teams to recover from individual map losses, reducing the significance of raw win-loss metrics"], "key_context": ["Match is BO3 format in playoffs, which differs from regular season group stage matches", "Both teams competing in VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs (B-Tier tournament)", "Recent matches occurred on April 5, 2026, suggesting current meta and roster stability", "Limited direct head-to-head history between UCAM and DNSTY in available search results", "Playoff stage typically features higher competitive intensity than regular season play"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T18:48:38.626535Z"}}, "resolution": null, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "cc5c917a-2fbb-459b-8c57-242f9a5cd3b0", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T18:50:30.006299+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1895724", "question": "Valorant: eSports Cologne vs Dortmund eSports - Map 1 Winner", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between eSports Cologne and Dortmund eSports in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 3:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"eSports Cologne\" if eSports Cologne win Map 1 against Dortmund eSports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dortmund eSports\" if Dortmund eSports win Map 1 against eSports Cologne.\n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and Map 1 is concluded with a winner determined, this market will resolve based on the completed Map 1. \n\nIf Map 1 is not completed for any reason, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all) or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without play beginning, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.24, "volume_usd": 15555.226564000002, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'search results provided do not contain specific information about a Valorant match between Cologne and Dortmund eSports' and provides no team performance data, roster information, or map pool strengths for either competitor. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: Current market pricing shows YES at 24% / NO at 76%, suggesting strong market belief in Dortmund eSports for Map 1. With zero objective data to contradict this, the market price becomes the only available signal. NO SUPPORTIVE DATA FOR YES: The 'Case for YES' section lists only gaps (insufficient data, no metrics, no preferences) rather than actual strengths favoring eSports Cologne. NO SUPPORTIVE DATA FOR NO: The 'Case for NO' section likewise contains only data gaps rather than actual evidence favoring Dortmund eSports; the market price reflects trader belief, not documented team strength. RESOLUTION CLARITY: The criteria are unambiguous \u2014 Map 1 winner determines resolution; if Map 1 completes, outcome is deterministic. No criteria ambiguity exists. MATCH TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~5 hours), making reversal highly unlikely and trading toward $0.01/$0.99 imminent regardless of official VLR.gg publication delay. CONFIDENCE CEILING: Because zero substantive team data exists in the briefing, both confidence scores are capped at 25. Market price alignment (24% \u2248 YES price) does not increase conviction when underlying data is entirely absent. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: Probability_score of 24 mirrors the current YES market price in the absence of countervailing evidence, reflecting true epistemic uncertainty rather than conviction in either direction.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no actionable data on either eSports Cologne or Dortmund eSports \u2014 search results reference unrelated VCL DACH teams (RIZON, CGN Esports) and Japanese Valorant competitions; match history, roster strength, map preferences, and head-to-head records are entirely absent, forcing reliance on market price as sole signal."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "NO (Dortmund) is heavily favored at 76% market price, indicating clear market consensus that Dortmund will win Map 1. The briefing contains critically insufficient data: no team rosters, recent match results, map pool strengths, veto preferences, or head-to-head records between Cologne and Dortmund are provided. Search results reference other VCL DACH teams (RIZON, CGN Esports) but contain no direct performance data for the Cologne vs Dortmund matchup. As the Bull advocating for the favored NO side (Dortmund), the market's 76% pricing suggests Dortmund possesses tangible competitive advantages\u2014likely recent form, roster strength, or map pool superiority\u2014that the briefing fails to articulate. Without access to opposing data, the underdog YES side (Cologne) appears weak primarily by elimination: if Dortmund commands 76% conviction, Cologne must lack comparable strengths, recent momentum, or map pool depth. EVENT TIMING is TODAY (~5 hours to resolution), leaving minimal time for momentum reversals or unexpected roster/tactical shifts; the market price reflects pre-match consensus unlikely to shift dramatically. The low confidence scores (YES: 22, NO: 28) reflect asymmetric data quality: briefing strongly supports the market's favorite (NO) through consensus pricing but provides zero direct evidence of either team's capabilities, creating genuine epistemic uncertainty on both sides. Market volume of $15,555 suggests moderate institutional participation; the 76% NO price is not an extreme outlier and likely reflects genuine analytical consensus, not panic or mispricing. Probability score of 76 for NO outcome (or equivalently, 24 for YES outcome) aligns with market price and the unavoidable logic that if one side is favored 3:1, the other is materially disadvantaged.", "key_factor": "Market consensus and institutional pricing favor Dortmund eSports at 76%, reflecting superior team composition or recent form not detailed in available briefing materials."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO actionable intelligence on either eSports Cologne or Dortmund eSports\u2014no recent match results, roster compositions, map pool strengths, head-to-head records, or current form data. The search results reference entirely different teams (RIZON, CGN Esports, Japanese competitors) in VCL DACH tournaments, but provide ZERO information about the Cologne vs Dortmund matchup scheduled for today. Market mispricing signal: A 76% NO price reflects high confidence in Dortmund's superiority, yet the briefing provides no data supporting or refuting this narrative. The 24% YES price appears artificially depressed. UNDERDOG CASE FOR YES: Without comparative performance data, the market's 3:1 confidence gap in Dortmund's favor is pure speculation. eSports Cologne could possess map veto advantages, superior recent form, or matchup-specific strengths entirely invisible to the market. Potential Cologne strength undetected by market: Early-season VCL DACH Stage 2 matches often favor teams with tight coordination and map-specific preparation\u2014factors invisible to a market relying on incomplete public data. Dortmund's fragility: The 76% pricing assumes Dortmund is a dominant favorite, yet the briefing reveals zero defensive weaknesses, recent losses, or roster instability that might explain the pricing premium. Market overconfidence is likely. Map 1 single-map context: Unlike best-of-three series, a single Map 1 introduces high variance. Veto mismanagement, map pool mismatches, or anti-meta positioning can flip expected outcomes with higher frequency than the 76% pricing implies. Murphy's Law applied to favorite: Dortmund's high pricing creates blind spots. Market participants may assume prior tournament performance translates directly to today's result without accounting for roster changes, meta shifts, or tactical evolution. Time urgency (5 hours to resolution): The event is LIVE/IMMINENT. No significant reversal-requiring events are likely before match start. However, this also means unpredictable in-game execution and map-specific matchup variance will dominate\u2014factors harder to price into a market lacking team data. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes=22 and confidence_no=24 reflect genuine uncertainty. Neither side has sufficient supporting evidence. The briefing's data vacuum prevents high-confidence analysis in either direction. Probability score of 28: Marginally above 25 (coin flip) to reflect that YES is the mathematical underdog AND appears underpriced relative to the absence of supporting data. A modest uptick from fair value suggests market inefficiency, not strong Cologne conviction.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum eliminates any rational basis for the 76% NO pricing, creating potential mispricing favoring the underdog."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.16, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing document contains zero actionable information about eSports Cologne or Dortmund eSports \u2014 no recent match results, roster data, map pool strengths, head-to-head history, or current form metrics are provided. Search results reference only unrelated VCL DACH matches (RIZON vs CGN Esports, Japanese regional teams) \u2014 no direct performance data for the target teams exists in the briefing. Market pricing at YES=24% / NO=76% is extreme and suggests strong consensus that Dortmund eSports is favored, but without underlying team data, we cannot validate whether this reflects genuine skill differential or sentiment distortion. TIMING RISK: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY classification). At this proximity to match start, market price has likely already incorporated available information. Reversal via late roster changes or technical issues is unlikely but resolution mechanism allows 50-50 if Map 1 incomplete. In single-map Valorant competitions, outcome variance is higher than best-of-series (map veto order, specific map pool strength, momentum carry-over are all compressed into one game). BASE RATE: Without team-specific data, neutral Valorant map-winner probability is ~50%. Market's 24% YES price indicates belief in ~3:1 underdog ratio for Cologne, but confidence cannot be justified without roster form, recent results, or head-to-head precedent. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: Cannot robustly evaluate either side (YES or NO) due to complete absence of comparative performance metrics. Both confidence scores deflated accordingly. Market price divergence from 50-50 baseline (24% vs typical 40-50% for close matches) is not explained by briefing data, suggesting either: (1) extensive off-chain research by market participants, (2) public knowledge not captured in search results, or (3) possible mispricing. RESOLUTION: Defer heavily to market consensus given data vacuum, but lower both confidence scores to reflect epistemic uncertainty. Probability_score anchored to market price but flagged as low-confidence estimate.", "key_factor": "Single map win probability in competitive Valorant eSports ~50% baseline for evenly matched teams; market pricing at 24/76 suggests substantial skill or form differential"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.2, "confidence_no": 0.2, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable information about eSports Cologne or Dortmund eSports\u2014no roster data, recent performance, map pools, head-to-head history, or veto preferences. Search results reference unrelated VCL DACH matches (RIZON vs CGN Esports, Japan tournaments) but not the target matchup, rendering comparative analysis impossible. Market price of 24% YES / 76% NO suggests Dortmund is heavily favored, but this conviction cannot be validated against the briefing\u2014no evidence supports either team's dominance. Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours with $15.5k volume; the match is imminent, leaving no time for new information to surface and correct any systematic mispricing. Asymmetric confidence reflects severe data scarcity: both sides equally unsupported by briefing evidence. Cannot justify conviction in either direction. Market may reflect offshore bookmaker consensus or pre-tournament seeding, but briefing provides no transparency into reasoning\u2014crowd psychology here is opaque, not detectable. No ignored signals detected because no signals exist in briefing. This is rational apathy born from information vacuum, not sentiment-driven mispricing. PROBABILITY SET TO 50: Genuine coin flip due to complete absence of discriminating evidence. Dortmund's 76% market share may be correct, but briefing offers no verification.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.15, "confidence_no": 0.15, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing references VCL DACH tournaments but provides zero match history, team rosters, or performance metrics for the two teams in question (Cologne vs Dortmund eSports). MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current market pricing (76% NO) suggests strong community confidence in Dortmund eSports, but without underlying performance data to validate this, the signal cannot be independently verified. EVENT TIMING CONSTRAINT: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours; insufficient time for meaningful reversal unless dramatic new information emerges (roster changes, forfeit, technical issues). MAP VETO BLINDNESS: Valorant map selection is strategically decisive (veto phases determine which maps favor which team compositions). No veto history or map pool data provided for either team. AGENT META ALIGNMENT: Team-specific agent pool strengths (Oper/Sentinel vs Initiator meta) cannot be assessed from briefing; this is a core factor in Map 1 win probability. ROSTER STABILITY UNKNOWN: No roster composition, recent roster changes, or player form metrics provided; players are core to competitive performance variance. NO PEER CONTEXT: Search results contain VCL DACH data for other teams (RIZON vs CGN) but not for the Cologne/Dortmund matchup, preventing cross-tournament benchmarking. CONFIDENCE SYMMETRY FAILURE: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set to 15 due to complete absence of directional evidence on either side\u2014this is a genuine data void, not a coin flip. MARKET STRUCTURE NOTE: At resolution (5 hours away), shares will trade at $0.01/$0.99 within minutes of outcome clarity; early positioning in a data-starved market is speculative.", "key_factor": "The briefing document contains no actionable data on either eSports Cologne or Dortmund eSports\u2014no roster composition, recent form, map pool strengths, agent meta alignment, or head-to-head history\u2014making meaningful probability estimation impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VOID: The briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either team\u2014no recent form, no roster composition, no map pool strengths, no head-to-head history, no individual player performance metrics. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES trading at 24% and NO at 76% suggests the market has conviction that Dortmund is favored, but this conviction is NOT backed by evidence in the briefing itself\u2014it reflects external knowledge or betting activity the council cannot verify. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. At this late stage, any roster disruption (illness, injury, technical issue with a player's setup) becomes a genuine black swan because substitution decisions must be made within minutes, not hours. ROSTER/LINEUP BLIND SPOT: The briefing is entirely silent on player health, recent absences, or stand-in availability for either team. In a BO3 map format, one player's substitution can swing map 1 by 5-15 rounds if the sub lacks familiarity with the team's veto strategy or agent pool. MAP VETO UNCERTAINTY: Without knowing which team bans/picks first, or which maps favor whom, the 76% NO conviction may rest on an assumption about map 1 outcome that could flip entirely if veto order or map selection favors Cologne's composition. MISSING META CONTEXT: No patch notes, agent buffs/nerfs, or recent tactical shifts mentioned. A meta change favoring Cologne's agent composition (e.g., Sage/Cypher durability buff) in the last 48 hours could explain underdog value. DORTMUND FATIGUE HYPOTHESIS: If Dortmund played yesterday or in a back-to-back series, they may enter this match with reduced prep time or morale disadvantage, undetected by aggregate stats but observable in first-map performance. COLOGNE UPSIDE: At 24%, the market may be underweighting a team that has shown improvement in recent weeks but whose latest wins fell outside the search window. Form trajectory matters in map 1 momentum. CONSENSUS TRAP: The 76% confidence in Dortmund is not grounded in briefing data\u2014it is inherited belief. If five other council members agree with the market price without evidence, they have all anchored to the same vacuum. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores set low because the briefing provides no ground truth for either side. A 28% probability score reflects only the market price signal and a slight Dortmund lean, but the absence of data means both sides are operating on guesswork.", "key_factor": "A key Cologne player falls ill or suffers a late injury just before match start, forcing an emergency roster sub who lacks map pool familiarity or clutch experience in this format."}], "final_score": 0.34887573964497043, "no_score": 0.6379775280898876, "edge": 0.10887573964497044, "no_edge": -0.1220224719101124, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 22% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1895724", "question": "Valorant: eSports Cologne vs Dortmund eSports - Map 1 Winner", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between eSports Cologne and Dortmund eSports in the VCL DACH: Evolution Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7