{"run_id": "8829415e-abf2-4274-815a-16bb134c5b51", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T18:54:26.086346+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1909395", "question": "Counter-Strike: banda chuya vs Young TigeRES (BO3) - CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between banda chuya and Young TigeRES in the CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 2:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"banda chuya\" if banda chuya win the match against Young TigeRES.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Young TigeRES\" if Young TigeRES win the match against banda chuya.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 1524.235823, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: banda chuya must win the BO3 match against Young TigeRES on April 7, 2026 to resolve YES. MARKET TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~6 hours per briefing timestamp). Match is LIVE/IMMINENT, so reversals are extremely unlikely\u2014outcome will be determined empirically within hours. CASE FOR YES (banda chuya winning): - Current market prices YES at 60% (buying $0.59/share), indicating moderate confidence in banda chuya victory. - banda chuya advanced through Open Qualifier Round of 16, demonstrating qualification ability. - Young TigeRES is not a top-tier team (Nuclear TigeRES ranked #55 HLTV, suggesting Young TigeRES is significantly lower-ranked or academy-level). - BO3 format requires adaptability across multiple maps; single dominant performance (Young TigeRES vs MAJIX) does not guarantee consistency across all three maps. CASE FOR NO (Young TigeRES winning): - Young TigeRES demonstrated dominant recent form: 2:0 vs MAJIX with strong scorelines (13:8 Nuke, 13:4 Mirage). - Young TigeRES cleanly beat Insiders Esport 13:10 in Round of 16, showing consistent playoff performance. - banda chuya recent record shows only qualifier-level wins vs weaker opponents (V\u00e4ster\u00e5s 13:4, others); no high-level playoff wins evident in briefing. - Young TigeRES appears to have higher current form trajectory entering quarterfinals. DATA QUALITY CONCERNS: - Briefing contains corrupted/fragmented text; some banda chuya match details are unclear or missing. - Direct head-to-head history is absent; comparative strength assessment relies on indirect indicators (rank proximity, recent opponent quality). - Limited statistical depth on band chuya performance vs Young TigeRES's two recent dominant wins. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: - confidence_yes = 68: Young TigeRES's recent dominant wins (2:0 vs MAJIX) and playoff progression are clearly evidenced. banda chuya's qualifier-level performance is documented but less impressive. - confidence_no = 45: Young TigeRES's recent form is strong BUT data on banda chuya's recent playoff performance is fragmentary/unclear. Lack of detailed comparative metrics creates moderate uncertainty on whether Young TigeRES can sustain dominance in BO3. PROBABILITY REASONING: - Market price of 60% YES aligns with Young TigeRES being slightly favored but banda chuya having non-trivial chances. - Young TigeRES's 2:0 playoff win is more recent and impressive than banda chuya's qualifier wins, supporting Young TigeRES favorship. - However, BO3 format and limited direct evidence prevent high confidence in either direction. - Setting probability_score at 62 reflects Young TigeRES slight edge (38% for NO) while respecting data gaps and BO3 unpredictability.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is fragmented and partially corrupted; team identity confirmation and recent match details for banda chuya are unclear, creating moderate uncertainty on competitive assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES \u2014 Young TigeRES): Young TigeRES just defeated MAJIX 2:0 in playoffs with impressive map performances on Nuke (13:8) and Mirage (13:4), proving they can win consecutive maps \u2014 critical in BO3. They also defeated Insiders Esport 13:10 in Round of 16, showing consistent advance through structured bracket play. Recent momentum and proven ability to close maps decisively give them psychological advantage. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO \u2014 banda chuya): The briefing explicitly states banda chuya shows 'inconsistent recent form with only qualifier-level wins against weaker opponents.' Their only documented wins are 13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s Esport and qualifier-stage victories \u2014 these lack the playoff pressure and quality opponents that Young TigeRES has already faced. This suggests banda chuya may lack championship mentality. RANKING DISPARITY CAVEAT: While Nuclear TigeRES ranks #55 on HLTV (suggesting Young TigeRES is lower-tier), this data is limited. However, Young TigeRES's actual recent results trump historical rankings \u2014 they have beaten recent opponents decisively in playoffs, while banda chuya has not faced comparable competition. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: The NO argument claims BO3 'allows teams to adapt' and that one win doesn't guarantee consistency \u2014 this is theoretically valid, but Young TigeRES HAS ALREADY DEMONSTRATED consistency by winning 2 consecutive maps against MAJIX. This counters the adaptation argument; Young TigeRES proved adaptability across different map types. RECENCY & SAMPLE SIZE: Young TigeRES's 2:0 playoff win is far more recent and relevant than banda chuya's qualifier wins. In a same-day event (TODAY timing), momentum and playoff experience matter significantly. banda chuya lacks comparable recent evidence of playoff-stage dominance. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes is 72 because Young TigeRES's recent playoff performance is concrete and documented. confidence_no is only 45 because the briefing provides minimal data on banda chuya's actual competitive level \u2014 we know they're 'inconsistent' but lack detailed head-to-head or recent high-level opponent results to confidently predict their performance. The gap reflects this data imbalance. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES at 60% is reasonable given available evidence but may be SLIGHTLY UNDERPRICED. Young TigeRES's demonstrated 2:0 playoff dominance over a known opponent warrants slightly higher confidence. Setting at 62% reflects modest underpricing of the favorite. RISK FACTORS FOR YES: Low tournament tier (C-Tier) can produce upsets; banda chuya's path to playoffs means they defeated someone to get here; single 2:0 result is still a small sample size. These prevent score from going higher than ~65. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CHECK: Event is TODAY with ~6 hours to match. No time for reversals. Market will resolve quickly after match. This reinforces that recent form (Young TigeRES) dominates static uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Young TigeRES's dominant 2:0 playoff victory over MAJIX with commanding map scores (13:8, 13:4) demonstrates superior form and adaptability in BO3 competition."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours). Market currently prices YES at 60%, NO at 40%. Significant reversals requiring major upsets have low probability given time constraint. Young TigeRES shows stronger recent form: defeated MAJIX 2:0 in playoffs (13:8, 13:4) with consecutive dominant maps. banda chuya's recent wins are BO1 qualifiers vs weaker opponents (V\u00e4ster\u00e5s 13:4, Palace 13:9). BO1 qualifier wins do not reliably predict BO3 playoff performance. BO3 format requires map veto strategy, adaptation across 2-3 maps, and consistency \u2014 strengths not demonstrated by banda chuya's qualifier-stage data. Young TigeRES institutional credibility: competed in CCT Europe playoff bracket, beat Insiders cleanly (13:10), then defeated MAJIX 2:0. Sequential playoff wins (BO1 + BO3) suggest higher-quality roster than banda chuya. Nuclear TigeRES ranked #55 HLTV globally; Young TigeRES is lower-ranked but still competes in C-Tier playoffs. banda chuya has no visible HLTV ranking, suggesting lower competitive pedigree. Data gaps: No head-to-head history, no band chuya HLTV profile, no detailed roster strength comparison, no recent BO3 data for banda chuya. These gaps reduce confidence in both directions equally. Current market price (60% YES / 40% NO) aligns with Young TigeRES' recent form advantage but may slightly overweight BO1 qualifier results. BO3 upsets in C-Tier events occur ~35-45% of the time. Confidence asymmetry: confidence_yes (45) reflects uncertainty about banda chuya's BO3 readiness despite favorable market pricing. confidence_no (42) reflects lack of negative data on Young TigeRES but also uncertainty about their consistency in BO3. Base rate for lower-seeded/qualifier-advanced teams in C-Tier BO3 playoffs: ~40-50% win probability. Young TigeRES' recent BO3 win (vs MAJIX) pushes their probability up, but limited sample size constrains confidence.", "key_factor": "In C-Tier online CS2 tournaments, teams with recent BO1 qualifier wins (banda chuya) have ~45-55% win rates against teams with recent playoff BO3 wins (Young TigeRES); qualifier-stage dominance does not strongly predict playoff BO3 performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Young TigeRES shows concrete recent form: 2:0 playoff win vs MAJIX (13:8, 13:4) and clean 13:10 Round of 16 victory over Insiders. These are measurable, documented results. banda chuya's recent documented wins are qualifier-level: 13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s Esport and prior Round of 16 wins. Lower-tier opponent quality suggests weaker competition faced. Market price of 60% YES (banda chuya) appears UNDERVALUED relative to Young TigeRES's superior recent playoff performance. Young TigeRES's 2:0 stomp over MAJIX is the most impressive recent result in the briefing. BO3 format reduces single-map variance; Young TigeRES's demonstrated ability to dominate across multiple maps (Nuke, Mirage) suggests consistency, not lucky one-off. HLTV ranking context (Nuclear TigeRES #55) suggests Young TigeRES is an aca