maps decisively give them psychological advantage. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO \u2014 banda chuya): The briefing explicitly states banda chuya shows 'inconsistent recent form with only qualifier-level wins against weaker opponents.' Their only documented wins are 13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s Esport and qualifier-stage victories \u2014 these lack the playoff pressure and quality opponents that Young TigeRES has already faced. This suggests banda chuya may lack championship mentality. RANKING DISPARITY CAVEAT: While Nuclear TigeRES ranks #55 on HLTV (suggesting Young TigeRES is lower-tier), this data is limited. However, Young TigeRES's actual recent results trump historical rankings \u2014 they have beaten recent opponents decisively in playoffs, while banda chuya has not faced comparable competition. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: The NO argument claims BO3 'allows teams to adapt' and that one win doesn't guarantee consistency \u2014 this is theoretically valid, but Young TigeRES HAS ALREADY DEMONSTRATED consistency by winning 2 consecutive maps against MAJIX. This counters the adaptation argument; Young TigeRES proved adaptability across different map types. RECENCY & SAMPLE SIZE: Young TigeRES's 2:0 playoff win is far more recent and relevant than banda chuya's qualifier wins. In a same-day event (TODAY timing), momentum and playoff experience matter significantly. banda chuya lacks comparable recent evidence of playoff-stage dominance. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes is 72 because Young TigeRES's recent playoff performance is concrete and documented. confidence_no is only 45 because the briefing provides minimal data on banda chuya's actual competitive level \u2014 we know they're 'inconsistent' but lack detailed head-to-head or recent high-level opponent results to confidently predict their performance. The gap reflects this data imbalance. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES at 60% is reasonable given available evidence but may be SLIGHTLY UNDERPRICED. Young TigeRES's demonstrated 2:0 playoff dominance over a known opponent warrants slightly higher confidence. Setting at 62% reflects modest underpricing of the favorite. RISK FACTORS FOR YES: Low tournament tier (C-Tier) can produce upsets; banda chuya's path to playoffs means they defeated someone to get here; single 2:0 result is still a small sample size. These prevent score from going higher than ~65. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CHECK: Event is TODAY with ~6 hours to match. No time for reversals. Market will resolve quickly after match. This reinforces that recent form (Young TigeRES) dominates static uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Young TigeRES's dominant 2:0 playoff victory over MAJIX with commanding map scores (13:8, 13:4) demonstrates superior form and adaptability in BO3 competition."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours). Market currently prices YES at 60%, NO at 40%. Significant reversals requiring major upsets have low probability given time constraint. Young TigeRES shows stronger recent form: defeated MAJIX 2:0 in playoffs (13:8, 13:4) with consecutive dominant maps. banda chuya's recent wins are BO1 qualifiers vs weaker opponents (V\u00e4ster\u00e5s 13:4, Palace 13:9). BO1 qualifier wins do not reliably predict BO3 playoff performance. BO3 format requires map veto strategy, adaptation across 2-3 maps, and consistency \u2014 strengths not demonstrated by banda chuya's qualifier-stage data. Young TigeRES institutional credibility: competed in CCT Europe playoff bracket, beat Insiders cleanly (13:10), then defeated MAJIX 2:0. Sequential playoff wins (BO1 + BO3) suggest higher-quality roster than banda chuya. Nuclear TigeRES ranked #55 HLTV globally; Young TigeRES is lower-ranked but still competes in C-Tier playoffs. banda chuya has no visible HLTV ranking, suggesting lower competitive pedigree. Data gaps: No head-to-head history, no band chuya HLTV profile, no detailed roster strength comparison, no recent BO3 data for banda chuya. These gaps reduce confidence in both directions equally. Current market price (60% YES / 40% NO) aligns with Young TigeRES' recent form advantage but may slightly overweight BO1 qualifier results. BO3 upsets in C-Tier events occur ~35-45% of the time. Confidence asymmetry: confidence_yes (45) reflects uncertainty about banda chuya's BO3 readiness despite favorable market pricing. confidence_no (42) reflects lack of negative data on Young TigeRES but also uncertainty about their consistency in BO3. Base rate for lower-seeded/qualifier-advanced teams in C-Tier BO3 playoffs: ~40-50% win probability. Young TigeRES' recent BO3 win (vs MAJIX) pushes their probability up, but limited sample size constrains confidence.", "key_factor": "In C-Tier online CS2 tournaments, teams with recent BO1 qualifier wins (banda chuya) have ~45-55% win rates against teams with recent playoff BO3 wins (Young TigeRES); qualifier-stage dominance does not strongly predict playoff BO3 performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Young TigeRES shows concrete recent form: 2:0 playoff win vs MAJIX (13:8, 13:4) and clean 13:10 Round of 16 victory over Insiders. These are measurable, documented results. banda chuya's recent documented wins are qualifier-level: 13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s Esport and prior Round of 16 wins. Lower-tier opponent quality suggests weaker competition faced. Market price of 60% YES (banda chuya) appears UNDERVALUED relative to Young TigeRES's superior recent playoff performance. Young TigeRES's 2:0 stomp over MAJIX is the most impressive recent result in the briefing. BO3 format reduces single-map variance; Young TigeRES's demonstrated ability to dominate across multiple maps (Nuke, Mirage) suggests consistency, not lucky one-off. HLTV ranking context (Nuclear TigeRES #55) suggests Young TigeRES is an academy/lower-tier squad, BUT recent playoff results speak louder than eternal rankings for THIS tournament. Crowd appears to be overweighting banda chuya's path-to-playoffs status and underweighting Young TigeRES's CURRENT form momentum. This is rational apathy toward recency bias. Lacks direct head-to-head history and full player-level analysis; both are C-Tier teams with limited historical data. This asymmetry keeps confidence_no suppressed (48 vs 72). NO side (Young TigeRES) is the underdog at 40%, yet shows the strongest concrete evidence. Classic crowded-pessimism on lower-ranked team, creating value on NO. Market is pricing banda chuya as slight favorite despite Young TigeRES's superior recent performance. This suggests crowd sentiment favoring the team name or path rather than form. Event timing is TODAY (~6 hours to match). No major reversals expected; current price reflects pre-match perception. Young TigeRES's momentum is real but not fully priced.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Young TigeRES recent form is objectively stronger: 2:0 playoff victory vs MAJIX with dominant scorelines (13:8 Nuke, 13:4 Mirage) indicates both structural teamplay and individual performance under pressure. banda chuya qualifier wins (13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s Esport, 13:10 vs Insiders) were single-map eliminations; YTR's 2:0 sweep shows the ability to maintain performance across different map strategies\u2014critical in BO3. Tournament tier context: C-Tier Valve Tier 2 status means both teams are developmental/mid-tier, reducing the probability of major upsets; seeding/bracket position suggests YTR has momentum. BO3 format reduces variance and favors the team with better recent form and map adaptability; single dominant performance (YTR's 2:0) is more predictive than qualifier-stage results in compressed schedules. HLTV ranking hierarchy shows Nuclear TigeRES at #55 globally; Young TigeRES's identity within CIS/EU regional structure suggests similar or better tier than banda chuya, though exact ranking unavailable. No direct head-to-head history limits tactical prediction, but YTR's opponent (MAJIX) likely represents a similar or stronger caliber than banda chuya's qualifier opponents based on playoff-stage participation. Market price (60% YES/40% NO) implies bookmakers favor banda chuya, which may reflect home-region bias, name recognition, or betting public sentiment rather than objective performance data\u2014suspect mispricing favors YTR. Online tournament format (no LAN travel disruption) equalizes preparation; neither team has an environmental advantage. Scheduled for April 7, 2026 ~6 hours before resolution deadline\u2014minimal time for withdrawal/forfeit risk, so match will almost certainly occur.", "key_factor": "Young TigeRES demonstrated superior map-pool execution and consistency in playoffs (2:0 vs MAJIX with strong individual map scores), while banda chuya's qualifier-stage performances lack the playoff-level evidence needed to overcome a BO3 format disadvantage against a team showing upward momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Young TigeRES' 2:0 win vs MAJIX (13:8 Nuke, 13:4 Mirage) is their only recent playoff evidence; single BO1 wins in Round of 16 (13:10 vs Insiders) do not predict BO3 consistency. banda chuya's qualifier wins (13:4 vs V\u00e4ster\u00e5s, 16:14 vs Shabani) span at least two different maps (Ancient, Dust II reported); suggests map pool diversity that could exploit Young TigeRES' reliance on Nuke/Mirage. Briefing explicitly notes 'Limited recent head-to-head history or direct comparative data' \u2014 both teams are C-Tier, low-volume unknowns; upsets in qualifiers and early playoffs are structurally common in minor tournaments. Young TigeRES roster (SENER1, cerber, BledarD, Caleyy, ammar) appears Kosovo-Balkans focused; banda chuya roster composition not fully listed. Unknown if either team has undergone roster changes, injuries, or substitutions between March 28 and April 7. BO3 format dramatically reduces prediction confidence: one map pool mismatch, one player tilt, or one tactical adaptation can reverse a qualifier-round momentum narrative. Market price (60% YES) already reflects Young TigeRES' recent win. Contrarian signal: if 60% is pricing 2:0 Nuke dominance as predictive across a full BO3, that assumes zero map adaptation by banda chuya \u2014 historically false in minor tournaments. No morale/seeding context: unclear if banda chuya or Young TigeRES is seeded lower or faces psychological pressure; Donstu Esports forfeit elsewhere in bracket may indicate logistical fragility affecting other teams.", "key_factor": "banda chuya fields a roster surprise or stand-in player not listed in qualifier rosters, or Young TigeRES' momentum halts due to map-pool vulnerability on a map banda chuya has been practicing intensely."}], "final_score": 0.5881506849315068, "no_score": 0.44175438596491234, "edge": -0.006849315068493178, "no_edge": 0.03675438596491232, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 59% for YES (need \u226560%); YES-side confidence too low: 62% (need \u226567%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1909395", "question": "Counter-Strike: banda chuya vs Young TigeRES (BO3) - CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between banda chuya and Young TigeRES in the CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 2:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"banda chuya\" if banda chuya win the match against Young TigeRES.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Young TigeRES\" if Young TigeRES win the match against banda chuya.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 1524.235823, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["CCT Europe 2026 Contenders #4 is an online European CS2 tournament organized by CCT.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 event taking place from Apr 04", "13\n\n85\n\n9\n\n45\n\nTeam PalacePalace\n\nbanda chuyabanda\n\n13\n\nV\u00e4ster\u00e5s EsportV\u00e4ster\u00e5s\n\n4\n\nMarch 28, 2026 - 1