{"run_id": "1068dc17-178c-44ff-b638-9472c2624ada", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T19:20:35.628002+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1909348", "question": "LoL: Misa Esports vs BIG (BO3) - EMEA Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket semifinal match between Misa Esports and BIG in the EMEA Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Misa Esports\" if Misa Esports win the match against BIG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BIG\" if BIG win the match against Misa Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 54818.01486700003, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "The briefing explicitly states 'search results contain information about Misa Esports' recent competitive performance in VALORANT tournaments... but do not provide specific information about a Misa Esports vs BIG League of Legends match in EMEA Masters 2026 Winter Playoffs.' All team performance data provided relates to VALORANT (VCL T\u00fcrkiye, VCL EMEA), not League of Legends. No information on Misa Esports' LoL roster, recent LoL results, or playoff seeding in EMEA Masters. No information whatsoever on BIG's LoL team, roster, recent form, or competitive standing. No head-to-head match history between Misa Esports and BIG in LoL. Without comparative team strength, recent form data, or roster information for either team, there is no evidentiary basis to assign a probability above or below 50. The market price (YES 58%, NO 42%) may reflect trader knowledge not present in this briefing, but per rules, analysis must be based ONLY on the provided briefing. Event timing is TODAY (resolves in ~5 hours), so reversal risk is irrelevant \u2014 the match is imminent or already occurring. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous: Misa Esports winning resolves YES, BIG winning resolves NO. Confidence is low on both sides due to complete absence of relevant LoL competitive data for either team.", "key_factor": "Critical data gap: Briefing contains only VALORANT performance data for Misa Esports and zero information on either team's LoL roster, recent form, head-to-head history, or competitive standing in EMEA Masters LoL \u2014 making any probability estimate above 50 impossible to justify."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains VALORANT match history for Misa Esports (VCL T\u00fcrkiye/EMEA), not League of Legends data. The LoL rosters, recent form, and competitive trajectory are completely absent. NO BIG INFORMATION: BIG's LoL team performance, roster composition, recent results, and playoff seeding are entirely missing from the briefing. Cannot assess relative strength. MARKET PRICING REFLECTS UNCERTAINTY: YES at 58% and NO at 42% suggests marginal favorite status, not dominant consensus. This pricing is consistent with information parity or slight market lean toward Misa without strong supporting data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: EMEA Masters 2026 Winter is A-Tier (March 9 - April 21). This is a Lower Bracket Semifinal, meaning both teams have already lost once. Both have tournament eligibility and stakes, but no seeding or bracket positioning data provided. EVENT TIMING - LIVE/IMMINENT: Match scheduled for April 7, 2:00 PM ET, resolving TODAY (~5 hours from briefing timestamp 2026-04-07 19:20 UTC). No time for catalysts; outcome likely already determined or nearly so. Market pricing may already reflect live betting or early result leaks. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Confidence on both sides is deliberately held LOW (28/25) because the briefing provides NO actionable LoL performance data for either team. Misa VALORANT success does not transfer to LoL predictive power. BIG's complete absence is a major blind spot. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT RATIONALE: Maintain market consensus (58% YES / 42% NO) because: (1) market makers have better information access than this briefing, (2) no contradictory evidence exists to overturn the favorite, (3) with ~5 hours to resolution, late movement suggests the market has already priced in available intel. YES at 58% is defensible as the slight favorite, but LOW confidence reflects data insufficiency, not conviction. WHY NOT HIGHER FOR YES: Misa's VALORANT inconsistency (recent 1-2 playoff losses in VCL EMEA, mixed Stage 2 results) does not prove LoL competence. BIG's complete absence from briefing means no weakness can be articulated\u2014unknown underdog risk exists. WHY NOT LOWER FOR YES: BIG team data gap cuts both ways; cannot confirm BIG is stronger. Market's 58-42 split is narrow, suggesting neither side has overwhelming evidence of superiority. Without LoL-specific competitive intel, deferring to market consensus is appropriate.", "key_factor": "Market pricing reflects underlying uncertainty; insufficient data prevents confident directional conviction on either side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.23, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains VALORANT statistics for Misa Esports (VCL T\u00fcrkiye/EMEA), not League of Legends performance. The LoL matchup is treated as a coin flip due to information vacuum, yet market prices YES at 58% \u2014 this is overconfidence without justification. BIG INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Zero data provided on BIG's roster, recent form, or competitive history. Market may be anchoring on Misa's brand recognition (from VALORANT success) while BIG remains an unexamined threat. Unknown opponents in elimination formats often outperform pricing. MISA'S RECENT LoL RECORD IS MIXED: Available match history shows Misa losing 1-2 in VCL EMEA playoffs (March 26-27 vs MDR and EP). Tournament performance data is sparse and shows recent setbacks, contradicting the 58% YES confidence. LOWER BRACKET DYNAMICS: This is a Lower Bracket Semifinal \u2014 both teams have already lost once. Misa's path to this stage is opaque; if they arrived here through losses, momentum may be negative. BIG's actual seeding and recent trajectory unknown. TOURNAMENT TIER DISCREPANCY: Search results conflate VCL (regional