{"run_id": "f5a8732d-0288-4064-8c79-17472ade64e1", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T19:59:52.977606+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1837437", "question": "LoL: 7REX vs Team Solid (BO1) - Circuito Desafiante Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between 7REX and Team Solid in the Circuito Desafiante Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"7REX\" if 7REX win the match against Team Solid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Solid\" if Team Solid win the match against 7REX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 15109.533419999998, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: 7REX must win the BO1 match scheduled for April 7 at 4:00 PM ET. CRITICAL DATA ISSUE: The briefing contains corrupted/garbled match table data with duplicate entries, incomplete rows, and unreadable formatting (e.g., 'Team Solid \"Team Solid\")Team Solid \"Team Solid\") Team Solid' repeated multiple times). HEAD-TO-HEAD AMBIGUITY: The match table shows both teams with entries containing 0-0 scores dated Apr 07, which may indicate the match hasn't occurred yet, is pending, or data is corrupted. TEAM STRENGTH ASSESSMENT IMPOSSIBLE: While briefing claims Team Solid is 0-2 overall and 7REX has one win (1-0 vs Ei Nerd), the corrupted data prevents reliable comparison of team rosters, recent form, or quality of opponents faced. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES (7REX) is trading at 58% vs NO (Team Solid) at 42%, suggesting modest confidence in 7REX but not overwhelming. This modest spread reflects genuine uncertainty. EVENT TIMING: Market resolves in ~6 hours (TODAY, April 7), and match is scheduled for 4:00 PM ET same day. Match timing is imminent with very limited opportunity for reversal. BOTH TEAMS WEAK: Both are 0-2, suggesting similar skill levels and high volatility in BO1 format; no clear favorite based on available evidence. CASE FOR 7REX: Has at least one documented win; market is pricing YES slightly higher, suggesting some analytics/expert consensus favors 7REX. CASE FOR TEAM SOLID: 0-2 record is same as 7REX; lack of evidence of clear inferiority; BO1 volatility means weaker team can easily win. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: Data corruption prevents confident analysis of either side. Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are LOW (~35) due to insufficient reliable information on team capabilities, head-to-head dynamics, or current form. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Market pricing (58/42) aligns with slight 7REX advantage from having one documented win. Without better data, deferring to market signal slightly adjusted to 52 (conservative, reflecting genuine coin-flip nature of match between two weak 0-2 teams).", "key_factor": "Briefing data is severely corrupted/malformed with duplicate team names, incomplete match records, and unclear head-to-head results; insufficient reliable information to differentiate team capabilities."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "YES CASE (Favored Side): 7REX has one documented win (1-0 vs Ei Nerd Esports on Apr 02), while Team Solid's 0-2 record shows zero victories across all matchups \u2014 this is the clearest differentiator supporting YES at 58%. YES CASE: In a BO1 format at the bottom tier of a developmental league, a team with demonstrated win capability (7REX) should be favored over a team with zero wins (Team Solid), even if margins are narrow. YES CASE: Market pricing at 58% reflects modest but meaningful confidence in 7REX \u2014 not an overconfident favorite, suggesting efficient pricing given limited data. NO COUNTERARGUMENT: Both teams are 0-2 in group stage standings, indicating statistically similar overall performance levels and competitive positioning. NO COUNTERARGUMENT: The briefing shows no head-to-head records between 7REX and Team Solid themselves in the group stage table \u2014 prior direct matchup data is unavailable, limiting confidence in relative matchup dynamics. NO COUNTERARGUMENT: Single wins in BO1 developmental league play carry limited predictive value; variance is high, and Team Solid's 0-2 could reflect unlucky scheduling or single-game flukes rather than skill gap. DATA QUALITY LIMITATION: The briefing table is fragmented and difficult to parse cleanly; exact win-loss records for each team require inference from partially displayed data. DATA QUALITY LIMITATION: No player roster analysis, recent form trends, or coaching changes are provided \u2014 only raw W-L records, limiting depth of confidence on either side. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=42 (moderate) because 7REX's single win is factual and 0-2 vs 1-0 is a concrete edge, but the sample size is tiny. confidence_no=35 (low) because Team Solid's weaknesses are clear (0-2 record) but alternatives (variance in BO1, unmeasured roster quality) lack supporting evidence. EVENT TIMING: Match resolves TODAY in ~6 hours \u2014 reversal scenarios (major injury, forfeit, technical issues) are theoretically possible but unlikely this close to start; confidence scores reflect a stable pre-match state.", "key_factor": "7REX has demonstrated at least one concrete victory (vs Ei Nerd Esports 1-0 on Apr 02) while Team Solid remains winless at 0-2 with no recorded victories in available data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH: Team Solid's 0-2 record does NOT reflect decisive losses to 7REX specifically\u2014the briefing shows their H2H matchup on Apr 07 was 0-0 (tied/unplayed at data cutoff), meaning they have not yet faced each other in this season. BRIEFING DATA GAP: The head-to-head table is fragmented and partially corrupted ('0-0' entries, unclear formatting), making it impossible to definitively extract 7REX vs Team Solid prior matchup records. This opacity cuts both ways but favors the underdog's narrative. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: The market's 58% confidence in 7REX rests heavily on their single 1-0 win vs Ei Nerd Esports (Apr 02), but Ei Nerd is also 0-2\u2014beating a 0-2 team once does not prove 7REX's consistency or meta-readiness for Team Solid specifically. BOTH TEAMS ARE EQUALLY WEAK: The briefing explicitly states both teams are 0-2 in standings with 'similar skill levels and form trajectories.' In developmental/academy-tier LoL, this means coin-flip matchups are common. The 58/42 split overstates 7REX's edge. BO1 VOLATILITY ADVANTAGE: Single-game elimination in a young, amateur league amplifies variance. Draft luck, early-game skirmish RNG, and meta-pocket picks matter more than long-form skill. Team Solid can steal a game through preparation or 7REX complacency. MARKET BIAS TOWARD NARRATIVE: The 'Case for YES' cherry-picks 7REX's one win while ignoring that Team Solid's losses are spread across diverse opponents (not a pattern vs specific teams). The market has anchored on 'slightly better roster' (unsubstantiated) rather than match data. MOMENTUM & RECENCY: 7REX's win was Apr 02; Team Solid's last result is unconfirmed at briefing cutoff (0-0 Apr 07). No recent form differential is documented. Both teams are equally uncertain. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY (6 hours away). If either team has technical issues, roster surprises, or forfeiture risk at academy level, the 50-50 tiebreaker clause becomes relevant\u2014this tail risk should slightly reduce YES confidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: The YES side has moderate justification (one head-to-head win proxy in 7REX beating Ei Nerd), but the briefing lacks match-specific intel (drafts, recent patches, player form). The NO side suffers from identical data scarcity, so confidence_no is only slightly higher\u2014both sides are under-informed. FINAL VERDICT: Market overprices 7REX's edge given two 0-2 teams with minimal recent H2H clarity and BO1 chaos. Team Solid is underpriced at 42%; a 45-55 range (favoring 7REX slightly but not decisively) better reflects the symmetry. Set probability_score = 38 to reflect NO upside while acknowledging 7REX's marginal form advantage.", "key_factor": "Team Solid's 0-2 record masks competitive head-to-head matchups with 7REX, and BO1 volatility in a developmental league creates high variance outcomes where the underdog can capitalize on single-game upsets."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "TEAM RECORDS: Both 7REX and Team Solid are 0-2 in group stage, indicating near-parity in skill/form. Historical base rate for BO1s between equally-ranked teams is ~50%, with slight edges awarded to teams with any demonstrable win. HEAD-TO-HEAD: The briefing shows no prior direct match between 7REX and Team Solid in the provided data. Head-to-head records in developmental leagues are unreliable predictors and carry minimal weight. MARGINAL EVIDENCE FOR 7REX: 7REX has one confirmed win (vs Ei Nerd Esports, Apr 02), while Team Solid's record shows 0-2 with no visible wins. This is the only concrete differentiator and justifies a modest edge (52% vs 50%). DEVELOPMENTAL LEAGUE VOLATILITY: Circuito Desafiante is a Brazilian qualifier/academy circuit with high variance, small rosters, and inconsistent team quality. Single-game BO1 results are highly unpredictable even with seeding data. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: YES at 58% vs base estimate of 52% suggests market is pricing in stronger confidence in 7REX than historical data supports. Market may be overweighting the single 7REX win or discounting Team Solid more than justified. DATA GAPS: No roster quality assessment, recent form trends, or head-to-head history provided. Cannot verify coaching, meta-game fit, or player performance metrics. Confidence capped at ~35-38 due to insufficient granular data. TIMING: Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours), leaving no time for news reversals. Current market pricing reflects final pre-game sentiment. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes set to 35 (weak support for 7REX edge); confidence_no set to 38 (slightly stronger due to parity argument, but both low due to data scarcity in developmental league context).", "key_factor": "In BO1 matches between similarly-ranked teams (both 0-2), the higher-seeded or marginally-favored team wins ~52-55% of the time; head-to-head records are weak predictors in developmental leagues with small sample sizes."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market price of 58% YES reflects a modest 16-point edge to 7REX, but briefing data is severely insufficient to justify confidence in either direction. Both teams are 0-2 in standings with nearly identical records; this alone suggests a near-coin-flip matchup (~50%), yet market has drifted to 58% YES. The 'CASE FOR YES' cites 7REX's 1-0 win vs Ei Nerd Esports (Apr 02), but this single data point is weak evidence; Team Solid's 0-2 record is matched by 7REX's 0-2 record. Head-to-head records in the briefing table show mixed/unresolved outcomes between these teams across the season; no clear pattern of 7REX dominance emerges. Critical data gap: The briefing contains NO recent form data, player availability, meta shifts, coaching changes, or team morale indicators that would differentiate two 0-2 teams. Crowd psychology signal: The 58% price may reflect overweighting of 7REX's single win (recency bias) while underweighting Team Solid's symmetry in losses; this is rational apathy masking as consensus. BO1 format + equivalent records = inherently unpredictable; a 50-55% edge is defensible but not robust given data scarcity. Confidence is LOW on both sides because the briefing offers no actionable differentiation between two struggling teams; market is essentially pricing a coin flip with a modest 7REX tilt. Volume of $15,110 is moderate and suggests retail participants; insufficient to suggest sophisticated edge-finding has occurred. Recommendation: 55% YES is a slight YES lean reflecting the minimal win-rate advantage, but both confidence scores remain depressed due to symmetrical information poverty.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Both 7REX and Team Solid are 0-2 in group stage \u2014 identical records indicate matched competitive levels, not a clear skill gap favoring either team. Head-to-head records are sparse and inconclusive; the briefing shows no direct 7REX vs Team Solid match result yet, limiting predictive power. 7REX's 1-0 win vs Ei Nerd Esports is offset by a 0-1 loss to Estral Esports on Mar 31; single wins in a 0-2 record do not establish dominance. Circuito Desafiante is a developmental/qualifier league with high variance; academy and lower-tier teams exhibit volatile performance week-to-week. BO1 format amplifies randomness compared to BO3/BO5; no series victory guarantees exist; tilt, meta shifts, and draft variance heavily influence single-game outcomes. Market pricing at 58% YES suggests marginal favoritism for 7REX, but briefing provides no roster, coaching staff, recent form trends, or patch-specific evidence to justify a >55% confidence. Data freshness is 2026-04-07 19:59 UTC; event resolves 2026-04-08 02:00 UTC (~6 hours remaining). No late-breaking injury, roster change, or veto news is available. Absence of individual player performance metrics, coach quality, or recent scrim results leaves confidence capped at ~45% on YES and ~42% on NO \u2014 insufficient domain-specific intelligence. Both teams' identical 0-2 records and lack of clear head-to-head precedent argue for near-parity; 54 probability reflects slight YES edge from market pricing, not fundamental evidence.", "key_factor": "Both teams are 0-2 with minimal head-to-head data; the market's 58% YES price for 7REX appears slightly overweighted given symmetric win records and the inherent variance of single-game BO1 formats in developmental leagues."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "SEVERE DATA GAPS: The briefing provides raw match tables and win-loss records but contains NO player-level statistics, recent form momentum, patch meta alignment, draft preferences, or coaching insights. Confidence on both sides must be artificially suppressed. BOTH TEAMS 0-2: Identical records mask entirely different trajectories\u2014one team could be on a momentum cliff while the other is stabilizing. The briefing offers no temporal signal (Are 7REX's losses getting closer? Is Team Solid's 2-0 start to April a reversal?) 7REX'S SINGLE WIN IS A MIRAGE: The 1-0 vs Ei Nerd (Apr 02) is cited as 'capability to win,' but Ei Nerd is also 0-2. Beating an equally struggling team provides zero predictive value in a BO1 coin-flip environment. MATCH HISTORY DATES ARE INCOHERENT: Head-to-head records show 7REX vs Team Solid dated Apr 07 with a '0-0' entry\u2014this could be a scheduled match NOT YET PLAYED, making the briefing's team comparison circular logic (we know 7REX beat Ei Nerd, so 7REX > Team Solid is invalid reasoning). ROSTER OPACITY: No mention of key player injuries, substitutions, or coaching changes. In a 6-hour window to match start, a visa denial, illness, or sub replacement for either team has outsized impact. The briefing silence on personnel suggests data availability gap, not absence of risk. META / PATCH UNKNOWN: No reference to recent LoL patch, item changes, or champion pool shifts. If April 7\u20138 patch favors control-heavy or engage-heavy play, Team Solid's playstyle preference could flip the matchup. This is a competitive factor entirely absent from briefing. MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Both 0-2, but are they mathematically eliminated? If 7REX has already clinched exit status and Team Solid has playoff hope (or vice versa), tilt and focus levels diverge dramatically in BO1. Briefing gives no playoff seeding context. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: YES at 58% vs NO at 42% is only a 16-point spread despite identical records and no differentiation data. This suggests the market is either (a) relying on narrative ('7REX has one win, so favored') or (b) acknowledging extreme uncertainty. If (b), 52 probability for YES is justified\u2014near-coin-flip with micro-edge to the narrative favorite. LIVE EVENT IMMINENT (6 hours): Roster changes, illness, or admin delays could emerge in the final hours. A reversal from 58\u219250-50 resolution is plausible if a player is benched or match rescheduled past 7-day window. CONFIDENCE DEPRESSION: With no player stats, no recent form separation, no meta data, and opaque roster status, confidence in either side must remain below 40. The 52 probability reflects slight YES lean from narrative ('7REX won once') rather than structural advantage.", "key_factor": "A critical player illness, visa issue, or last-minute roster substitution on 7REX forces them to field a sub or play at reduced capacity, negating their marginal edge."}], "final_score": 0.5145744680851064, "no_score": 0.49534246575342467, "edge": -0.07042553191489354, "no_edge": 0.08034246575342463, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 40% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1837437", "question": "LoL: 7REX vs Team Solid (BO1) - Circuito Desafiante Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between 7REX and Team Solid in the Circuito Desafiante Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"7REX\" if 7REX win the match against Team Solid.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Solid\" if Team Solid win the match against 7REX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins du