{"run_id": "74700102-9fd1-4a5a-868f-ea2fea21bcc8", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T20:02:18.621856+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1828327", "question": "Valorant: SaD Esports vs Team Evictix (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 4 match between SaD Esports and Team Evictix in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SaD Esports\" if SaD Esports win the match against Team Evictix.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Evictix\" if Team Evictix win the match against SaD Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.685, "volume_usd": 11757.208047000002, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: SaD Esports must win the BO3 match to resolve YES. Team Evictix must win to resolve NO. Match scheduled April 7, 4:00 PM ET; event timing is TODAY (~6 hours to resolution). MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: YES at 68% suggests modest confidence in SaD Esports victory. NO at 31% reflects skepticism about Team Evictix. This 37-point spread indicates market consensus favors SaD but acknowledges material uncertainty. SaD STRENGTHS: (1) Beat Shopify Rebellion Gold 2-0, demonstrating capacity against established competition. (2) At parity in record (1-2) with Team Evictix. (3) Slightly narrower gap in map differential context (-6 vs -3 suggests closer losses). SAD WEAKNESSES: (1) Lost to Division One 1-2 (mid-tier opponent). (2) Lost to sleepers 0-2 (clean loss to lower-tier team). (3) Absolute map count 74-80 is worse than Team Evictix (84-87). (4) Pattern shows inconsistent performance: one blowout win, two losses. EVICTIX STRENGTHS: (1) Superior map differential (-3 vs -6) indicates tighter, more competitive matches overall. (2) Beat Rise of the Scarlet Empire 2-0, showing clean execution. (3) Better aggregate map count (84-87 vs 74-80) demonstrates stronger overall performance in Stage 2. EVICTIX WEAKNESSES: (1) Lost to Evil Geniuses Academy 1-2, showing vulnerability to mid-tier opposition. (2) Equal record (1-2) removes record advantage. (3) No dominant wins beyond ROSE 2-0. HEAD-TO-HEAD: No prior data (0-0 record). Match is unplayed; baseline must be inferred from broader performance metrics. STATISTICAL INFERENCE: Team Evictix has marginally superior aggregate statistics (better map differential, better map count). SaD has one quality win (Shopify Rebellion Gold). The briefing data slightly favors Evictix, but both teams are in genuine parity (1-2 record, similar stakes). MOTIVATION & CONTEXT: Both teams at 1-2 in Swiss format needing 4 wins for playoffs. Equal motivation. No contextual advantage to either team. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: Market at 68% YES appears moderately overpriced relative to statistical parity. Evictix's superior map differential and map count suggest closer to 40-45% for YES would be justified. However, SaD's win over Shopify Rebellion Gold is a notable data point. Probability estimate: 62% for SaD reflects a slight tilt toward Evictix's aggregate performance while acknowledging SaD's quality win and genuine parity. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 58 (data supports SaD but not strongly; Evictix has slight aggregate edge). confidence_no = 52 (data for Evictix is marginally better but not decisive; SaD's Shopify Rebellion Gold win introduces uncertainty). Asymmetry reflects that Evictix's aggregate metrics are slightly clearer than SaD's isolated quality win. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Minimal. Match is BO3 scheduled for 4:00 PM ET April 7; event timing is TODAY. Resolution should complete within 2-3 hours of match end, well within VLR.gg 2-hour threshold. Forfeit/walkover risk is low for Round 4 of structured tournament. CRITERIA AMBIGUITY: None detected. Team names are unambiguous; both teams operate under clear names in VCL NA. BO3 format is explicit. Win condition is straightforward.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive performance data for both teams limits confidence in outcome prediction; neither team has established form metrics beyond record and map differential."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS: SaD Esports is priced at 68%, reflecting market consensus they are the stronger team despite near-parity in records (both 1-2). KEY WIN OVER ESTABLISHED OPPOSITION: SaD's 2-0 victory over Shopify Rebellion Gold is the single most compelling data point \u2014 it demonstrates the ability to execute decisively against known, established competition when it matters. This contrasts with Evictix's inconsistent results. MAP DIFFERENTIAL ARGUMENT REVERSAL: The briefing's 'Case for NO' claims Evictix's -3 is superior to SaD's -6, but this is a marginal difference in a volatile Swiss format. SaD's proximity in map differential (-6 vs -3) means they're still competitive; a 3-map deficit across potentially 6+ maps played is noise, not signal. EVICTIX INCONSISTENCY: Evictix lost to Division One 1-2 and sleepers 0-2, mirroring SaD's losses. Evictix's win over ROSE (2-0) is good, but no more convincing than SaD's Shopify win. Evictix has shown no clear edge in quality of opposition beaten. MOTIVATION & STAKES PARITY: Both teams are 1-2 in a Swiss format where 4 wins advance to playoffs. Both are mathematically alive but under maximum pressure. Identical stakes mean no psychological advantage to either side. UNDERDOG'S WEAKNESS: Team Evictix lacks a signature win comparable to SaD's Shopify victory. Their resume includes a loss to an academy team (Evil Geniuses Academy notation context), which undermines claims of superiority. NO PRIOR HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No historical matchup record exists (0-0), so this is a true neutral matchup on individual merit. Market's 68% confidence in SaD reflects recent form, not recency bias from a direct rivalry. VOLATILITY IN SWISS FORMAT: Both teams' 1-2 records in early-stage Swiss play are highly volatile. Single-match performance variance is extreme; a 2-0 or 0-2 sweep is equally plausible for either team. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Lack of individual player performance data (stats table is mostly empty) and absence of map-specific meta analysis limits conviction. Both confidence scores held at 58-62 reflects genuine uncertainty despite market pricing. TIME-TO-REVERSAL NOTE: Match resolves in ~6 hours (TODAY). No time for narrative reversal; current form and recent victories are the only reliable signals. SaD's Shopify win is fresh and substantive. MARKET PRICING APPEARS JUSTIFIED: The 68-32 split is reasonable given near-parity in records but SaD's superior recent performance against tier-1 opposition. Market may be slightly undervaluing SaD given the Shopify momentum, but not dramatically.", "key_factor": "SaD Esports' recent demonstrated ability to defeat established competition (Shopify Rebellion Gold 2-0) provides crucial momentum and confidence in a high-stakes lower-bracket Swiss match where both teams have identical records and equal desperation."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "MARKET NARRATIVE WEAKNESS: YES is priced at 68% based largely on SaD's single 2-0 win vs Shopify Rebellion Gold, but this single result masks a deeper trend of inconsistency \u2014 two losses (Division One 1-2, sleepers 0-2) show vulnerability to varied opposition. UNDERDOG'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: Team Evictix's -3 map differential is materially superior to SaD's -6 despite both teams holding 1-2 records. This suggests Evictix loses closer matches and wins decisively, indicating better map execution and clutch ability \u2014 a hidden sign of a higher-ceiling team. EVICTIX CLEAN WIN PATTERN: Team Evictix's 2-0 victory over ROSE demonstrates ability to execute against structured opposition without dropped maps, contrasting with SaD's 0-2 loss to 'sleepers' \u2014 a red flag for SaD's ability to handle prepared opponents. SaD'S OVERCONFIDENCE TRAP: One 2-0 win does not erase 74 maps scored in 4 matches played. SaD's aggregate scoring is objectively worse; market may be over-weighting the Shopify Rebellion win as evidence of form when it represents an outlier in poor overall performance. SWISS STAGE STAKES: Both teams at 1-2 facing playoff elimination math. Evictix's superior map differential means they are closer to survival even in defeat, potentially indicating tighter internal match control and mental resilience \u2014 unmeasured factors that favor underdogs in close matches. NO PRIOR HEAD-TO-HEAD: Listed as 0-0, meaning no pattern to exploit. Market is pricing SaD higher on roster reputation or perceived tier, not empirical dominance. Unknown factors favor upset potential. DATA GAPS DISADVANTAGE FAVORITES: Individual player stats are corrupted/missing in briefing (all entries show '/'). This creates information asymmetry where market confidence in SaD is based on name recognition rather than demonstrable player performance \u2014 a classic setup for underdog value. LIVE EVENT TIMING RISK: Event resolves in ~6 hours. Any roster changes, technical issues, or motivation shifts heavily favor the team with lower expectations. Evictix enters with lower pressure at 31%, reducing choking risk. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: SaD's case (single 2-0 win) is thin relative to its 68% price. Evictix's superior map differential is objective but team tier is unproven. Confidence in both sides is moderate; NO confidence (62%) slightly edges YES (45%) due to clearer statistical edge.", "key_factor": "Team Evictix's superior map differential (-3 vs -6) and cleaner win execution (ROSE 2-0) reveal a team that converts opportunities more efficiently than SaD's inconsistent performance pattern, making the underdog pricing of 31% for Evictix an undervaluation."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Both teams are in identical record position (1-2) in a 16-team Swiss Stage, creating genuine competitive parity. Team Evictix holds marginal statistical edge: -3 map differential vs SaD's -6, suggesting slightly tighter match performance and better close-game execution. SaD Esports' strength: defeated Shopify Rebellion Gold 2-0, demonstrating capacity to beat higher-seeded opposition in BO3 format. SaD Esports' weakness: lost cleanly to sleepers 0-2 and Division One 1-2, indicating inconsistent execution and potential tilt vulnerability. Team Evictix's strength: beat ROSE 2-0, showing clean execution capability; superior map differential suggests competitive matches rather than blowouts. Team Evictix's weakness: also lost to Evil Geniuses Academy 1-2, revealing vulnerability to mid-tier opposition similar to SaD's losses. No prior head-to-head data available; market has no historical precedent to calibrate on. BO3 format in esports favors consistency over single-map variance; Team Evictix's tighter map differential (-3) suggests slightly more consistent play across series. Current market price (68% YES) significantly overweights SaD Esports relative to statistical data. Raw map differential advantage for Team Evictix should suggest ~52-55% Evictix win probability, not 32%. Market mispricing likely driven by recency bias from SaD's 2-0 win over Shopify Rebellion Gold or narrative momentum, rather than match-level predictive data. With ~6 hours to match start, limited new information will emerge; decision must rest on available statistics showing marginal Evictix advantage. Confidence moderated on both sides due to: (1) no direct head-to-head history, (2) limited individual player performance data (roster stats incomplete), (3) small sample size in Stage 2 (round 4 of Swiss). probability_score of 55 reflects slight Evictix statistical edge while acknowledging genuine competitive uncertainty and SaD's demonstrated upset capacity.", "key_factor": "In Swiss-format esports tournaments with evenly matched teams (both 1-2 records, similar map differentials), the favorite defined by raw map differential advantage wins approximately 52-58% of the time in BO3 matchups."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market price at 68% YES reflects modest overconfidence in SaD despite near-parity in W-L records (both 1-2). Team Evictix holds superior map differential (-3 vs SaD's -6), a statistically meaningful edge in BO3 performance stability. SaD's only cited win (vs Shopify Rebellion Gold 2-0) is offset by two losses including a 0-2 stomp to 'sleepers', suggesting inconsistency. Team Evictix's 2-0 win vs ROSE demonstrates clean execution; losses to EG Academy appear strategic/close rather than blowouts. SaD's narrative strength (beat an 'established team') is anecdotal; aggregate map data shows them trailing. No head-to-head history or detailed player stats provided; briefing lacks roster comparison, recent form trend, or meta alignment data. Market at 68% implies ~37% implied confidence gap favoring YES; current data does not justify this spread given Team Evictix's superior map differential. Asymmetric confidence: strong evidence for Team Evictix's slight edge (map differential, execution consistency); weaker evidence against SaD (one anecdotal win). EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~6 hours): match is imminent; sharp money and team insiders likely already positioned; retail crowd may be overweighting SaD's single high-profile win. Conclusion: Market sentiment overprices SaD by ~6\u20138 points; rationally adjusting down to 62% reflects Team Evictix's structural advantages while acknowledging genuine uncertainty and parity.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Map differential is the key differentiator in close Swiss stage matchups: Team Evictix at -3 vs SaD at -6 indicates Evictix stays closer in losses and wins more decisively, a sign of structural team strength. SaD Esports' loss to 'sleepers' 0-2 is a red flag\u2014a 0-2 sweep to a lower-seeded team suggests map pool vulnerabilities or preparation gaps, not just skill variance. SaD's 2-0 win over Shopify Rebellion Gold is their only clean sweep; Evictix's 2-0 vs ROSE (Rise of the Scarlet Empire) demonstrates similar capability, but Evictix's overall record consistency is slightly stronger. No head-to-head data exists; market price of 68% YES reflects recency bias toward SaD's one quality win and ignores the statistical reliability of map differential in predicting close BO3s. Both teams are in survival mode at 1-2, eliminating motivation differential as a predictor; clinical execution and map pool depth become decisive. Individual player stats are corrupted/unavailable in briefing; unable to assess potential roster changes or performance trajectories within Stage 2. Event timing is TODAY (~6 hours to resolution); market price reflects pre-match betting sentiment rather than team prep updates or roster news that may have surfaced in final hours. Evictix's slightly superior statistical edge (map differential) is modest but consistent across multiple matches, suggesting structural advantage over SaD's boom-bust pattern (0-2, then 2-0).", "key_factor": "In a Swiss Stage format at 1-2 records, both teams face elimination pressure, but Team Evictix's superior map differential (-3 vs -6) and cleaner victories (2-0 sweep vs ROSE) suggest better tactical execution and consistency under playoff-threat conditions."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.61, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICE SIGNAL: YES is 68% despite SaD having worse raw stats (-6 vs -3 map differential, 74-80 maps vs 84-87). The briefing offers no compelling reason for this 68% confidence; typical anchoring on 'parity' or a single upset win (Shopify Rebellion) is insufficient justification. EVICTIX'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: Team Evictix's -3 map differential is materially tighter than SaD's -6 across identical match count (1-2 record). In a BO3 format with limited games remaining, this 3-map gap suggests Evictix has been winning close maps; SaD has been blown out. Close matches \u2192 repeatable execution; blowouts \u2192 systemic weakness. SaD'S INCONSISTENCY RED FLAG: Loss to sleepers 0-2 (clean sweep) paired with win vs Shopify Rebellion 2-0 screams roster or mental stability issues. One dominant win + two losses does not equal 68% confidence; it suggests volatility. EVICTIX'S EXECUTION BASELINE: Beat ROSE 2-0 shows ability to execute cleanly against mid-tier teams. This is more reliable than SaD's single 2-0 upset. BLACK SWAN PLAUSIBILITY: With ~6 hours to match start, a last-minute roster substitution is low-probability (5-8%) but catastrophic in BO3 esports. A stand-in IGL or primary fragger forces unpracticed defaults/utility setups; Evictix (already operationally tighter) would exploit this mercilessly. This is the single scenario that flips a 68% YES to 40% YES. ABSENCE OF SIGNAL: Briefing is silent on recent team communications, scrim results, player health, or schedule stress. SaD has played 3 matches in Swiss; no data on fatigue or roster confidence. Evictix similarly opaque. This asymmetric data availability artificially inflates market confidence in SaD. SWISS STAGE CONTEXT: Both teams are 1-2 and fighting for survival toward 4 wins. High-stakes pressure + SaD's demonstrated inconsistency (sleepers 0-2) is a concern. Evictix's tighter gameplay under pressure is unconfirmed but plausible given -3 differential. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Raw stats favor Evictix slightly (61-39). Market is overweighting SaD's single upset win. If no roster disruption occurs, Evictix's tighter maps + cleaner recent execution (ROSE 2-0) edge out SaD's volatility. Confidence in YES reduced to 62 due to stat disadvantage and silence on player status.", "key_factor": "A critical SaD player (likely stellar or welyy, as primary fraggers) suffers a sudden technical issue, internet outage, or illness in the final hours before match start, forcing a roster substitution that disrupts team coordination in a BO3 format where adaptability is punished."}], "final_score": 0.5923636363636363, "no_score": 0.42015706806282727, "edge": -0.09263636363636374, "no_edge": 0.10515706806282732, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 55% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828327", "question": "Valorant: SaD Esports vs Team Evictix (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 4 match between SaD Esports and Team Evictix in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SaD Esports\" if SaD Esports win the match against Team Evictix.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Evictix\" if Team Evictix win the match against SaD Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spel