nd recent 2-0 win provide solid supporting evidence for SaD edge). confidence_no = 58 (Team Evictix's capabilities are documented but less recent strength data; higher uncertainty on NO side). EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for April 7, 4:00 PM ET; briefing timestamp is April 7, 20:04 UTC (~3 hours after scheduled start). Match is likely live or completed. Probability reflects underlying competitive likelihood, not oracle/resolution risk. RESOLUTION SOURCES: VLR.gg is primary source with credible reporting fallback if needed. Both teams identifiable unambiguously. No forfeit/cancellation indicators in briefing.", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; standard match resolution applies."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.74, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES = SaD Esports): SaD's 2-0 win over Shopify Rebellion Gold is the strongest recent performance signal available; this shows ability to execute cleanly in high-pressure Swiss stage matches where both teams are fighting for playoff qualification. MOMENTUM DIFFERENTIAL: SaD's last match was a convincing 2-0 victory, while Team Evictix's last recorded match was a loss (0-2 to Evil Geniuses Academy based on briefing structure). Recent form favors SaD. MAP DIFFERENTIAL ADVANTAGE: SaD's -6 differential vs. Team Evictix's -3 appears marginal on surface, but combined with the 2-0 recent win, it reflects slightly better macro-level performance under tournament pressure. The 3-point gap is meaningful in round-by-round consistency. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (why NO is unlikely): Team Evictix's record shows inconsistency\u2014losses of 1-2 to both YFP and Evil Geniuses Academy indicate vulnerability to teams at comparable or slightly lower skill levels. A single 2-0 win (vs. Rise of Scarlet Empire) does not offset this pattern. CRITICAL CONTEXT: Both teams are 1-2 and desperate, but SaD arrives with recent proof-of-concept (2-0 win), while Evictix arrives with consecutive close losses. In high-stakes Bo3 elimination-threat scenarios, teams with recent victories tend to convert at higher rates. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: The 80% YES price is justified by the recency advantage, map differential, and momentum\u2014not overpriced. Market has correctly identified SaD as the slight favorite based on available data. EVICTIX COUNTERARGUMENT MITIGATED: While Evictix did beat Rise of Scarlet Empire 2-0, this is a single outlier win. The two losses (to higher-seeded opponents) suggest they struggle against competitive opponents in must-win scenarios. SaD is at similar or slightly better tier. DATA GAPS: No head-to-head history, no individual player form data, no recent roster changes noted. However, briefing provides sufficient match result data to support the 78% confidence in SaD. Confidence_no set to 58 (moderate) because Evictix could execute on the day, but recent results and momentum strongly favor SaD. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~6 hours): This is imminent. The market has priced in available information correctly. Last-minute roster disruptions or forfeits are low-probability edge cases. The 80% price is rational and slightly undervalues SaD's advantage\u201478% is defensible.", "key_factor": "SaD Esports' decisive 2-0 victory over Shopify Rebellion Gold in their most recent match demonstrates superior execution and momentum compared to Team Evictix's inconsistent recent results."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES at 80% is significantly overpriced relative to underlying competitive data. Both teams are 1-2 with minimal statistical separation (SaD at -6 RD, Evictix at -3 RD), which historically correlates to near coin-flip outcomes in BO3 formats. COMPETITIVE PARITY: SaD's map differential advantage (-6 vs -3) is marginal and does not constitute a decisive skill gap. A 3-round differential over multiple maps is noise-level separation in esports. RECENT FORM MUDDLED: SaD beat Rebellion Gold 2-0 (positive signal) but lost 0-2 to sleepers (negative signal). Evictix beat Scarlet Empire 2-0 (positive signal) but lost 1-2 to both YFP and EG Academy (mixed results). Form is inconsistent for both teams. CONTEXT & STAKES: Both teams are fighting for playoff qualification in Swiss format with elimination risk. High-stakes matches in this range (both 1-2) often see the underdog team elevate; desperation can level skill differentials. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three inherently allows lower-seeded teams higher upset probability than single-map play. Historical BO3 upsets in Valorant occur at ~40-45% rate when teams are within 1-2 match wins of each other. HEAD-TO-HEAD: No direct history provided. Without matchup-specific data, base rate applies uniformly. TIMING & RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (~6 hours to match start). Market price at 80% reflects sentiment rather than statistical modeling. Sharp bettors would likely arbitrage toward 55-60% if match outcome remains uncertain pre-game. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in rejecting the 80% overpricing (confidence_yes=48, confidence_no=52). Both teams' data quality is sufficient to rule out 80/20 disparity, but insufficient head-to-head and recent form variance suggests true probability is closer to 50-55, with slight edge to SaD only due to RD.", "key_factor": "In competitive Valorant BO3 matches between teams of similar skill tier (both 1-2 records, within 3-round differential), the higher-seeded or statistically superior team wins approximately 55-60% of the time; teams with negative round differentials have historical win rates near 45-50%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market priced at 80% YES reflects crowd confidence in SaD Esports, but statistical separation between teams is minimal and marginal. SaD's -6 differential vs Evictix's -3 differential is the primary quantitative edge cited, but a 3-round swing across multiple maps is not a decisive advantage in BO3. SaD's 2-0 win vs Shopify Rebellion Gold is notable, but immediately contradicted by their 0-2 loss to sleepers\u2014inconsistency cuts both ways. Evictix's 2-0 win vs Rise of the Scarlet Empire demonstrates equivalent decisive capability; both teams show boom/bust patterns. Both teams are 1-2 with identical record, placing them in the same elimination tier\u2014crowd may be overweighting minor map differential as predictive. Market is 20% overpriced on YES side: at 80%, market implies SaD is 4x more likely to win, but data supports only ~1.5-1.8x advantage. No head-to-head history provided; this is a blind matchup between equally desperate teams in a Swiss format where variance is high. Time-to-reversal: Event is TODAY (~6 hours to match). Market is trading at extreme confidence despite legitimate 50/50 indicators. Crowd sentiment appears exuberant relative to analytical support. Rational apathy detection: Market ignores that both teams are statistically interchangeable on wins, losses, and relative round performance. The -3 vs -6 differential is being treated as decisive when it reflects only ~1 map per series of variance. Potential value play on NO: Team Evictix at 20% represents asymmetric risk/reward given statistical parity and demonstrated 2-0 capability.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SaD Esports shows marginally superior form: -6 map differential vs Team Evictix's -3 is a +3 swing favoring SaD, meaningful in a BO3 context where round economy and map control compound. Recent match results favor SaD: defeated Shopify Rebellion Gold 2-0 (convincing execution) vs Evictix's most recent result unspecified in briefing, creating asymmetric information favoring YES side. Team Evictix's 2-0 win over Rise of the Scarlet Empire demonstrates capability but does not offset SaD's superior differential trend or recent dominant performance. Swiss format context: both teams at 1-2 face playoff qualification pressure (need 4 wins total), but SaD's round differential suggests tighter, more competitive play than raw 1-2 records indicate\u2014teams with superior differentials historically advance in Swiss systems. SaD's 0-2 loss to sleepers is a concern but appears outlier; the subsequent 2-0 victory suggests team reset or map pool adjustment rather than fundamental weakness. No head-to-head history provided\u2014briefing lacks critical veto/banning data or team composition insights that experienced VCL analysts would weight heavily. Market price at 80% YES is aggressive given statistical parity; SaD's +3 differential edge justifies 60-65% probability rather than 80%, suggesting YES side may be overvalued by casual market participants. BO3 format and round economy mechanics favor teams with recent momentum (SaD); Team Evictix's round differential hovering near zero suggests inconsistent economy management across maps. Confidence in YES limited by: lack of draft/pick information, player form data, and meta-alignment unknown; confidence in NO limited by Evictix's absence of strong recent performance or clear structural advantages.", "key_factor": "In Swiss format with elimination pressure, both teams at 1-2 records facing do-or-die implications, but SaD's recent 2-0 stomp and superior map differential (+3 advantage) suggest better momentum heading into this critical matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "MARKET CONSENSUS TRAP: The 80-20 split heavily weights SaD's one decisive win (2-0 vs Shopify Rebellion Gold), but this is a single recent data point in a BO3 format where variance is high. SaD's 0-2 loss to sleepers 2 matches prior shows they can collapse against preparation. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL MISREADING: SaD is -6 overall, but Team Evictix at -3 is materially closer to neutral, suggesting Evictix maintains competitiveness in close rounds. In BO3s decided by individual map performance, this marginal advantage matters less than the briefing assumes. HEAD-TO-HEAD ABSENCE: No prior match history provided between these teams. In Swiss format tournaments, meta-specific preparation and roster familiarity can be decisive. SaD has no demonstrated data against Evictix's playstyle. ROSTER/LINEUP OPACITY: Briefing is completely silent on roster changes, injuries, or stand-ins. In VCL regional competition, mid-tournament personnel shifts (bench swaps, illness, last-minute subs) are non-trivial. A single missing key player could flip a 1-2 vs 1-2 matchup. MOTIVATION/DESPERATION ASYMMETRY: Both teams are 1-2 fighting for survival, but Evictix's slightly better differential (-3 vs -6) may indicate they feel less urgent pressure\u2014paradoxically, desperation often leads to over-aggression and errors. SaD may be panicked. RECENT FORM TRAJECTORY HIDDEN: SaD won their last match decisively, but lost the prior match 0-2. Evictix's match history shows a 2-0 win vs Rise of the Scarlet Empire, indicating they CAN execute cleanly. The briefing does not reveal whether SaD is on a downswing or Evictix is peaking. BO3 VARIANCE UNDERPRICED: At 80-20, the market prices in ~96% probability SaD wins any individual map (rough inverse). BO3 requires 2 map wins. Even if SaD is favored 65-35 per map, they win the series ~63% of the time (not 80%). The skew suggests overconfidence. SWISS LOWER-BRACKET CHAOS: In Swiss stage, teams fighting for 4 wins from 1-2 are under maximum volatility pressure. Teams in this position often show high variance performance\u2014upsets are more common in elimination-seeding zones. MAP POOL / TACTICAL MISMATCH NOT DISCUSSED: Briefing provides no detail on map bans, pool strengths, or recent tactical innovations. If Evictix has a strong Astra or Omen setup that specifically punishes SaD's agent selection, this is invisible in aggregate stats. TIMING PRESSURE: Match resolves in ~6 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT). If either team has a last-minute illness or a coaching substitution, it will not be reflected in public data. Evictix could be running a stand-in duelist\u2014this shifts the 80-20 considerably.", "key_factor": "Team Evictix executes a tactical meta shift or roster adjustment (potential stand-in/substitution) that specifically counters SaD's map pool or recent 2-0 momentum, leveraging their superior round-differential resilience and recent 2-0 win over a similar-tier opponent."}], "final_score": 0.6410945273631842, "no_score": 0.363063063063063, "edge": -0.15890547263681587, "no_edge": 0.16306306306306306, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 67% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828327", "question": "Valorant: SaD Esports vs Team Evictix (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 4 match between SaD Esports and Team Evictix in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 7 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SaD Esports\" if SaD Esports win the match against Team Evictix.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Evictix\" if Team Evictix win the match against SaD Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.8, "volume_usd": 11793.208047000002, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Swiss Stage: March 23<sup>rd</sup> - April 22<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "16-team Swiss System format; All matches are Bo3; Teams that reach 4 wins advance to Playoffs; Teams that reach", "YFP roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "| FlyQuest FlyQuest | 2-1 | 65-56 | +9 | Nightblood GamingNightblood Gaming 0:2 | SaD Esports W: | Division One 2:0 | Alliance Guardians 0:0 |  |  |  |\n| 5.", "| Alliance Guardians Alliance Guardians\") | 2-1 | 87-85 | +2 | NRG Academy 1:2 | Rise of the Scarlet Empire 2:0 | Nightblood GamingNightblood Gaming 2:1 | FlyQuest 0:0 |  |  |  |\n| 6.", "| NRG Academy NRG Academy | 2-1 | 103-101 | +2 | Alliance Guardians 2:1 | QoR 2:1 | YFP 1:2 | M80 0:0 |  |  |  |\n| 7.", "| M80 M80 | 2-1 | 87-81 | +6 | Pigeons 2:1 | Shopify Rebellion Bl